WEBVTT

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:27.087
[MAN SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY
OVER RADIO]

00:01:46.273 --> 00:01:48.692
Bloody kids.

00:02:35.197 --> 00:02:38.701
MAN: How fastidious you've become,
Wormtail.

00:02:38.909 --> 00:02:43.247
As I recall, you once called
the nearest gutter pipe home.

00:02:43.414 --> 00:02:45.249
Could it be that the task of nursing me...

00:02:46.792 --> 00:02:48.627
...has become wearisome for you?

00:02:48.794 --> 00:02:51.255
Oh, no. No, no, my Lord Voldemort.

00:02:51.422 --> 00:02:52.715
I only meant...

00:02:52.923 --> 00:02:55.926
...perhaps if we were to do it
without the boy.

00:02:56.093 --> 00:02:58.304
No! The boy is everything!

00:02:58.596 --> 00:03:02.141
It cannot be done without him.
And it will be done.

00:03:02.266 --> 00:03:05.060
Exactly as I said.

00:03:05.311 --> 00:03:09.148
-I will not disappoint you, my Lord.
VOLDEMORT: Good.

00:03:09.273 --> 00:03:12.276
First, gather our old comrades.

00:03:12.443 --> 00:03:14.737
Send them a sign.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:29.919
VOLDEMORT: Nagini tells me
the old Muggle caretaker...

00:03:30.169 --> 00:03:33.672
...is standing just outside the door.

00:03:33.923 --> 00:03:39.219
Step aside, Wormtail, so I can give
our guest a proper greeting.

00:03:39.303 --> 00:03:41.221
Avada Kedavra!

00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:47.686
HERMIONE: Harry.
-Ah!

00:03:48.437 --> 00:03:50.230
Harry!

00:03:51.398 --> 00:03:53.233
Are you all right?

00:03:54.026 --> 00:03:56.153
Hermione. Bad dream.

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:59.531
-When did you get here?
-Just now. You?

00:03:59.698 --> 00:04:01.075
Last night.

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:03.327
Wake up! Wake up, Ronald!

00:04:03.577 --> 00:04:04.828
Bloody hell.

00:04:05.079 --> 00:04:06.455
Honestly, get dressed.

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:09.083
And don't go back to sleep.

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:12.461
Come on, Ron!
Your mother says breakfast's ready!

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:20.719
HARRY:
Ron, where are we actually going?

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:22.096
RON:
Don't know.

00:04:22.429 --> 00:04:25.724
-Hey, Dad. Where are we going?
-Haven't the foggiest.

00:04:25.975 --> 00:04:27.351
Keep up!

00:04:30.104 --> 00:04:31.855
MAN:
Arthur!

00:04:32.106 --> 00:04:34.108
It's about time, son.

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:38.487
Sorry, Amos. Some of us
had a bit of a sleepy start.

00:04:38.737 --> 00:04:41.240
This is Amos Diggory, everyone.

00:04:41.323 --> 00:04:44.326
Works with me at the Ministry.

00:04:44.868 --> 00:04:47.204
And this strapping young lad
must be Cedric, am I right?

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:48.372
Yes, sir.

00:04:48.622 --> 00:04:50.290
This way.

00:04:52.084 --> 00:04:55.295
Merlin's beard!
You must be Harry Potter.

00:04:55.504 --> 00:04:58.298
-Yes, sir.
-Great, great pleasure.

00:04:58.424 --> 00:05:00.384
Pleasure to meet you too, sir.

00:05:02.928 --> 00:05:05.556
AMOS:
Yes, it's just over there.

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:09.685
ARTHUR: Shall we?
AMOS: Oh, yeah.

00:05:09.852 --> 00:05:11.270
ARTHUR:
We don't want to be late.

00:05:11.395 --> 00:05:15.399
AMOS: Come on. Nearly there now.
Get yourself into a good position.

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:18.694
Why are they all standing around
that manky old boot?

00:05:18.861 --> 00:05:21.405
-That isn't just any manky old boot.
-It's a Portkey.

00:05:21.447 --> 00:05:22.865
AMOS:
Time to go!

00:05:23.073 --> 00:05:24.575
What's a Portkey?

00:05:24.867 --> 00:05:28.871
-Ready! After three. One, two...
-Harry!

00:05:29.079 --> 00:05:30.247
...three!

00:05:41.258 --> 00:05:42.301
Let go, kids!

00:05:42.426 --> 00:05:44.428
-What?!
ARTHUR: Let go!

00:05:57.232 --> 00:05:59.610
I'll bet that cleared your sinuses, eh?

00:06:00.778 --> 00:06:03.405
AMOS: Total shambles, as per usual.
-Thanks.

00:06:09.119 --> 00:06:11.288
ARTHUR:
Go on, look at that!

00:06:11.455 --> 00:06:15.918
Well, kids, welcome to
the Quidditch World Cup!

00:06:18.921 --> 00:06:21.507
ARTHUR:
Stay together! Keep up, girls!

00:06:23.133 --> 00:06:24.468
Look!

00:06:25.427 --> 00:06:27.471
ARTHUR:
Come on! Keep up, girls!

00:06:31.016 --> 00:06:32.935
Whoa!

00:06:33.519 --> 00:06:35.854
-Aah!
-Blimey!

00:06:36.021 --> 00:06:37.940
Parting of the ways, I think, old chap.

00:06:38.148 --> 00:06:39.483
-See you at the match.
-See you.

00:06:39.525 --> 00:06:40.943
-Cedric.
-Ced, come on.

00:06:41.151 --> 00:06:42.820
FRED:
See you later, Cedric.

00:06:43.445 --> 00:06:45.030
Ah.

00:06:47.491 --> 00:06:49.493
Home sweet home.

00:06:51.453 --> 00:06:52.830
HARRY:
What?

00:07:00.045 --> 00:07:02.172
ARTHUR: Excellent, excellent.
HERMIONE: Ginny, look!

00:07:02.464 --> 00:07:03.882
ARTHUR: All to the bath.
HERMIONE: Look.

00:07:04.049 --> 00:07:06.468
Girls, choose a bunk and unpack.

00:07:06.885 --> 00:07:09.388
Ron, get out of the kitchen.
We're all hungry.

00:07:09.513 --> 00:07:11.056
FRED AND GEORGE:
Get out of the kitchen!

00:07:11.348 --> 00:07:14.518
-Feet off the table!
FRED AND GEORGE: Feet off the table!

00:07:15.561 --> 00:07:17.855
I love magic.

00:07:33.036 --> 00:07:36.373
VENDOR: Get your Quidditch World Cup
programs here!

00:07:36.707 --> 00:07:39.835
Blimey, Dad. How far up are we?

00:07:40.043 --> 00:07:41.378
LUCIUS:
Well, put it this way:

00:07:41.712 --> 00:07:43.380
If it rains...

00:07:43.547 --> 00:07:45.924
...you'll be the first to know.

00:07:46.717 --> 00:07:49.178
Father and I are in
the minister's box...

00:07:49.344 --> 00:07:52.431
...by personal invitation
of Cornelius Fudge himself.

00:07:52.723 --> 00:07:54.850
Don't boast, Draco.

00:07:55.058 --> 00:07:57.227
There's no need with these people.

00:07:59.563 --> 00:08:02.232
Do enjoy yourself, won't you?

00:08:02.441 --> 00:08:04.401
While you can.

00:08:10.407 --> 00:08:12.743
Yeah! Yeah!

00:08:17.748 --> 00:08:19.708
AMOS:
Come on up. Take your seats.

00:08:19.875 --> 00:08:22.419
I told you these seats
would be worth waiting for.

00:08:22.586 --> 00:08:24.421
Come on!

00:08:26.757 --> 00:08:28.592
FRED:
It's the Irish! There's Troy!

00:08:28.884 --> 00:08:30.594
GEORGE: And Mullet!
FRED: And Moran!

00:08:36.433 --> 00:08:39.394
CROWD [CHANTING]:
Ireland! Ireland! Ireland!

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:46.610
GEORGE: Here come the Bulgarians!
FRED: Yes!

00:08:46.902 --> 00:08:48.278
ALL:
Whoa!

00:08:52.783 --> 00:08:54.243
GINNY:
Who's that?

00:08:54.910 --> 00:08:57.913
That, sis, is the best Seeker
in the world.

00:08:59.998 --> 00:09:03.460
CROWD [CHANTING]:
Krum! Krum! Krum!

00:09:08.257 --> 00:09:09.466
HARRY, RON, FRED AND GEORGE:
Krum!

00:09:09.633 --> 00:09:12.135
-Yes!
-Whoo!

00:09:19.142 --> 00:09:21.019
Good evening!

00:09:21.478 --> 00:09:24.481
As Minister for Magic...

00:09:24.815 --> 00:09:27.818
...it gives me great pleasure...

00:09:28.485 --> 00:09:32.322
...to welcome
each and every one of you...

00:09:32.489 --> 00:09:38.328
...to the final
of the 422nd Quidditch World Cup!

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:40.330
Let the match...

00:09:40.539 --> 00:09:42.332
...begin!

00:09:48.463 --> 00:09:50.507
RON AND HARRY CHANTING:
Krum! Krum! Krum!

00:09:52.676 --> 00:09:56.305
[FRED AND GEORGE
SINGING GIBBERISH]

00:09:58.473 --> 00:10:00.058
There's no one like Krum.

00:10:00.309 --> 00:10:01.810
FRED: Krum?
-Dumb Krum?

00:10:01.977 --> 00:10:05.063
He's like a bird,
the way he rides the wind.

00:10:05.314 --> 00:10:08.191
-He's more than an athlete.
-Dumb Krum.

00:10:08.358 --> 00:10:09.568
He's an artist.

00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:11.987
-I think you're in love, Ron.
RON: Shut up.

00:10:12.321 --> 00:10:13.572
[SINGING]
Viktor, I love you

00:10:13.864 --> 00:10:15.490
Viktor, I do

00:10:15.532 --> 00:10:18.076
When we're apart
My heart beats only for you

00:10:19.536 --> 00:10:21.580
Sounds like the Irish
have got their pride on.

00:10:21.872 --> 00:10:23.540
ARTHUR:
Stop! Stop it!

00:10:24.207 --> 00:10:25.709
It's not the Irish.

00:10:26.877 --> 00:10:29.004
We've gotta get out of here. Now!

00:10:31.214 --> 00:10:33.550
MAN:
Get out, it's the Death Eaters!

00:10:33.592 --> 00:10:37.012
Get back to the Portkey, everybody,
and stick together!

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:39.890
Fred, George!
Ginny is your responsibility.

00:10:40.515 --> 00:10:42.225
Go!

00:10:42.517 --> 00:10:44.227
Harry!

00:10:48.023 --> 00:10:49.941
[DEATH EATERS
CHANTING INDISTINCTLY]

00:10:59.034 --> 00:11:01.244
GEORGE: Keep up, you lot!
-Harry!

00:11:02.537 --> 00:11:04.581
Harry! Harry!

00:11:52.295 --> 00:11:53.630
Morsmordre!

00:12:20.615 --> 00:12:21.992
RON:
Harry!

00:12:23.618 --> 00:12:26.663
-Where are you?
HERMIONE: Harry!

00:12:27.831 --> 00:12:30.667
RON:
We've been looking for you for ages!

00:12:31.668 --> 00:12:33.628
Thought we lost you, mate.

00:12:34.337 --> 00:12:36.339
HARRY:
What is that?

00:12:39.509 --> 00:12:41.553
WIZARDS:
Stupefy!

00:12:41.678 --> 00:12:42.971
ARTHUR:
Stop!

00:12:43.138 --> 00:12:45.474
That's my son!

00:12:46.516 --> 00:12:49.060
-Ron, Harry, Hermione, you all right?
-We came back for Harry.

00:12:49.227 --> 00:12:50.562
Which of you conjured it?

00:12:50.687 --> 00:12:52.856
-Crouch, you can't possi--
-Do not lie!

00:12:53.064 --> 00:12:55.066
You've been discovered
at the scene of the crime.

00:12:55.233 --> 00:12:57.235
-Crime?
-Barty! They're just kids.

00:12:57.527 --> 00:12:58.862
What crime?

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:01.573
It's the Dark Mark, Harry.
It's his mark.

00:13:01.698 --> 00:13:02.866
What, Voldemort?

00:13:04.075 --> 00:13:07.871
Those people tonight, in the masks,
they're his too, aren't they?

00:13:08.163 --> 00:13:10.373
-His followers?
-Yeah.

00:13:10.665 --> 00:13:12.542
Death Eaters.

00:13:13.168 --> 00:13:17.172
-Follow me.
-There was a man, before.

00:13:17.714 --> 00:13:19.007
There!

00:13:19.174 --> 00:13:21.676
All of you, this way!

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:23.720
ARTHUR:
A man, Harry?

00:13:23.887 --> 00:13:25.555
Who?

00:13:25.764 --> 00:13:27.724
I don't know.

00:13:29.267 --> 00:13:31.561
I didn't see his face.

00:13:47.744 --> 00:13:49.746
WOMAN:
Anything from the trolley?

00:13:51.748 --> 00:13:54.918
Anything from the trolley?

00:13:58.797 --> 00:14:00.632
Anything from the trolley, dears?

00:14:00.757 --> 00:14:02.926
RON:
Packet of Drooble's...

00:14:03.218 --> 00:14:04.928
...and a Licorice Wand.

00:14:06.555 --> 00:14:08.598
On second thought, just the Drooble's.

00:14:08.765 --> 00:14:12.769
-It's all right, I'll get it. Don't worry.
-Just the Drooble's. Thanks.

00:14:13.937 --> 00:14:16.439
Two Pumpkin Pasties, please.

00:14:21.778 --> 00:14:23.446
Thank you.

00:14:23.947 --> 00:14:26.241
WOMAN:
Anything sweet for you, dear?

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:29.452
Oh, no, I'm not hungry. Thank you.

00:14:30.328 --> 00:14:32.330
WOMAN:
Anything from the trolley?

00:14:32.581 --> 00:14:34.624
HERMIONE:
This is horrible.

00:14:34.791 --> 00:14:37.669
How can the Ministry
not know who conjured it?

00:14:37.794 --> 00:14:39.629
Wasn't there any security or...?

00:14:39.796 --> 00:14:42.632
Loads, according to Dad.

00:14:42.799 --> 00:14:46.761
That's what worried them so much.
Happened right under their noses.

00:14:49.264 --> 00:14:52.684
It's hurting again, isn't it?
Your scar.

00:14:52.809 --> 00:14:54.644
I'm fine.

00:14:56.646 --> 00:14:59.482
You know Sirius will
want to hear about this...

00:14:59.774 --> 00:15:03.778
...what you saw at the World Cup
and the dream.

00:15:11.995 --> 00:15:15.290
Hedwig. There we go.

00:15:54.412 --> 00:15:56.831
Clear the runway!

00:15:59.709 --> 00:16:01.878
-Aah!
ALL: Whoa!

00:16:02.045 --> 00:16:04.881
Well, there's something
you don't see every day.

00:16:28.905 --> 00:16:31.366
DUMBLEDORE: Well, now we're all
settled in and sorted...

00:16:31.574 --> 00:16:33.910
...I'd like to make an announcement.

00:16:34.911 --> 00:16:38.206
This castle will not only be
your home this year...

00:16:38.373 --> 00:16:41.584
...but home to some
very special guests as well.

00:16:41.918 --> 00:16:44.462
You see, Hogwarts has been chosen....

00:16:45.463 --> 00:16:46.923
Yes, what is it?

00:16:47.090 --> 00:16:48.591
What is it?

00:16:50.927 --> 00:16:54.222
Tell them to wait.
Tell them to wait. Wait.

00:16:54.389 --> 00:17:00.395
So Hogwarts has been chosen
to host a legendary event:

00:17:00.603 --> 00:17:02.605
The Triwizard Tournament.

00:17:02.939 --> 00:17:05.108
-For those of you who do not know...
BOTH: Brilliant.

00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:08.611
...the Triwizard Tournament
brings together three schools...

00:17:08.778 --> 00:17:10.822
...for a series of magical contests.

00:17:10.947 --> 00:17:14.492
From each school, a single student
is selected to compete.

00:17:14.784 --> 00:17:16.411
Now let me be clear.

00:17:16.619 --> 00:17:19.497
If chosen, you stand alone.

00:17:19.789 --> 00:17:21.624
And trust me when I say...

00:17:21.916 --> 00:17:24.919
...these contests are not
for the faint-hearted.

00:17:24.961 --> 00:17:29.424
But more of that later.
For now, please join me in welcoming...

00:17:29.632 --> 00:17:31.968
...the lovely ladies of the
Beauxbatons Academy of Magic...

00:17:33.803 --> 00:17:37.807
...and their headmistress,
Madame Maxime.

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:51.946
RON:
Bloody hell.

00:17:59.829 --> 00:18:01.998
Blimey. That's one big woman.

00:18:24.020 --> 00:18:26.064
And now our friends from the north.

00:18:26.356 --> 00:18:29.067
Please greet the proud sons
of Durmstrang...

00:18:29.359 --> 00:18:32.028
...and their high master,
Igor Karkaroff.

00:18:55.093 --> 00:18:56.886
STUDENT:
Oh, it's Krum!

00:18:57.053 --> 00:18:58.388
Blimey, it's him!

00:18:58.596 --> 00:19:00.431
Viktor Krum!

00:19:09.399 --> 00:19:10.900
KARKAROFF:
Albus.

00:19:11.067 --> 00:19:12.735
Igor.

00:19:26.249 --> 00:19:29.961
Professor Dumbly-dorr,
my horses have traveled a long way.

00:19:30.086 --> 00:19:32.755
-They will need attending to.
-Don't worry, Madame Maxime.

00:19:32.922 --> 00:19:36.384
Our gamekeeper, Hagrid,
is more than capable of seeing to them.

00:19:36.551 --> 00:19:38.928
MAXIME:
But you know, Monsieur Hagrid...

00:19:39.262 --> 00:19:41.639
...they drink only single-malt whiskey.

00:19:43.057 --> 00:19:44.267
Ah!

00:19:48.062 --> 00:19:49.564
You idiot!

00:19:54.485 --> 00:19:56.487
DUMBLEDORE:
Your attention, please!

00:19:58.656 --> 00:20:00.700
I'd like to say a few words.

00:20:02.869 --> 00:20:04.871
Eternal glory.

00:20:05.246 --> 00:20:09.250
That is what awaits the student
who wins the Triwizard Tournament.

00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:13.755
But to do this, that student
must survive three tasks.

00:20:14.005 --> 00:20:17.842
Three extremely dangerous tasks.

00:20:18.217 --> 00:20:20.637
BOTH: Wicked.
DUMBLEDORE: For this reason...

00:20:20.887 --> 00:20:23.723
...the Ministry has seen fit
to impose a new rule.

00:20:23.890 --> 00:20:25.141
To explain all this...

00:20:25.391 --> 00:20:29.020
...we have the head of the Department
of International Magical Cooperation...

00:20:29.103 --> 00:20:31.272
...Mr. Bartemius Crouch.

00:20:45.787 --> 00:20:48.414
RON:
Bloody hell. It's Mad-Eye Moody.

00:20:49.165 --> 00:20:52.418
-Alastor Moody? The Auror?
-Auror?

00:20:52.669 --> 00:20:56.089
Dark-wizard catcher. Half the cells
in Azkaban are filled thanks to him.

00:20:56.881 --> 00:21:00.051
He's supposed to be mad as a hatter,
though, these days.

00:21:11.688 --> 00:21:15.400
-My dear old friend, thanks for coming.
-Stupid ceiling.

00:21:15.566 --> 00:21:16.776
Thank you.

00:21:23.157 --> 00:21:25.118
What's that he's drinking,
do you suppose?

00:21:25.535 --> 00:21:28.538
I don't know, but I don't think
it's pumpkin juice.

00:21:35.461 --> 00:21:37.422
CROUCH:
After due consideration...

00:21:37.588 --> 00:21:40.466
...the Ministry has concluded that,
for their own safety...

00:21:40.717 --> 00:21:43.594
...no student under the age of 17...

00:21:43.845 --> 00:21:47.557
...shall be allowed to put forth their
name for the Triwizard Tournament.

00:21:47.724 --> 00:21:50.351
-This decision is final.
FRED: That's rubbish!

00:21:50.601 --> 00:21:53.146
That's rubbish!
You don't know what you're doing!

00:21:53.312 --> 00:21:57.150
-Silence!
-They're not too happy about that, then.

00:22:16.502 --> 00:22:19.005
The Goblet of Fire.

00:22:19.505 --> 00:22:22.341
Anyone wishing to submit themselves
to the tournament...

00:22:22.508 --> 00:22:25.386
...need only write their name
upon a piece of parchment...

00:22:25.636 --> 00:22:28.765
...and throw it in the flame before
this hour on Thursday night.

00:22:29.891 --> 00:22:32.143
Do not do so lightly.

00:22:32.393 --> 00:22:36.105
If chosen, there's no turning back.

00:22:36.189 --> 00:22:41.194
As from this moment,
the Triwizard Tournament has begun.

00:23:07.386 --> 00:23:09.305
Alastor Moody.

00:23:11.224 --> 00:23:13.017
Ex-Auror...

00:23:14.644 --> 00:23:17.146
...Ministry malcontent...

00:23:17.230 --> 00:23:19.690
...and your new
Defense Against the Dark Arts teacher.

00:23:19.899 --> 00:23:24.237
I am here because Dumbledore asked me.
End of story, goodbye, the end.

00:23:24.445 --> 00:23:26.239
Any questions?

00:23:29.325 --> 00:23:31.244
When it comes to the Dark Arts...

00:23:32.453 --> 00:23:35.206
...I believe in a practical approach.

00:23:35.289 --> 00:23:41.212
But first, which of you can tell me
how many Unforgivable Curses there are?

00:23:41.587 --> 00:23:43.965
-Three, sir.
-And they are so named?

00:23:44.215 --> 00:23:47.260
Because they are unforgivable.
The use of any one of them will--

00:23:47.468 --> 00:23:51.597
Will earn you a one-way ticket
to Azkaban, correct.

00:23:51.848 --> 00:23:54.475
The Ministry says you're too young
to see what these curses do.

00:23:54.725 --> 00:23:58.187
I say different! You need to know
what you're up against!

00:23:58.271 --> 00:24:00.481
You need to be prepared.

00:24:00.690 --> 00:24:03.192
You need to find another place
to put your chewing gum...

00:24:03.276 --> 00:24:05.570
...besides the underside of your desk,
Mr. Finnigan!

00:24:05.736 --> 00:24:08.739
No way. The old codger
can see out the back of his head.

00:24:09.448 --> 00:24:11.284
MOODY:
And hear across classrooms!

00:24:13.619 --> 00:24:17.206
So which curse shall we see first?

00:24:17.290 --> 00:24:18.457
-Weasley!
-Yes?

00:24:18.624 --> 00:24:20.084
Stand.

00:24:23.254 --> 00:24:25.006
Give us a curse.

00:24:25.256 --> 00:24:29.010
Well, my dad did tell me about one.

00:24:29.510 --> 00:24:30.761
The Imperius Curse.

00:24:31.012 --> 00:24:34.307
Oh, yeah, your father
would know all about that.

00:24:34.640 --> 00:24:37.310
Gave the Ministry quite a bit of grief
a few years ago.

00:24:37.768 --> 00:24:40.313
Perhaps this will show you why.

00:24:47.987 --> 00:24:49.322
Hello.

00:24:50.907 --> 00:24:52.533
Lovely little beauty.

00:24:55.745 --> 00:24:57.747
Engorgio.

00:24:58.164 --> 00:24:59.790
Imperio!

00:25:04.295 --> 00:25:06.547
MOODY:
Don't worry. It's completely harmless.

00:25:12.803 --> 00:25:14.388
If she bites...

00:25:15.056 --> 00:25:16.432
...she's lethal.

00:25:19.060 --> 00:25:20.811
What are you laughing at?

00:25:22.313 --> 00:25:23.564
Get off!

00:25:26.067 --> 00:25:27.818
Talented, isn't she?

00:25:28.027 --> 00:25:31.364
What should I have her do next?
Jump out the window?

00:25:33.366 --> 00:25:34.700
Drown herself?

00:25:46.462 --> 00:25:49.799
Scores of witches and wizards
have claimed...

00:25:49.966 --> 00:25:53.970
...that they only did
You-Know-Who's bidding...

00:25:54.220 --> 00:25:56.389
...under the influence
of the Imperius Curse.

00:25:56.472 --> 00:25:58.391
But here's the rub:

00:25:58.808 --> 00:26:01.811
How do we sort out the liars?

00:26:04.230 --> 00:26:05.856
Another, another.

00:26:06.857 --> 00:26:08.401
Up, up. Come on.

00:26:08.484 --> 00:26:10.194
Longbottom, is it?

00:26:10.736 --> 00:26:12.363
Up.

00:26:14.407 --> 00:26:18.202
Professor Sprout tells me
you have an aptitude for herbology.

00:26:20.121 --> 00:26:21.747
There's the....

00:26:21.998 --> 00:26:23.874
The Cruciatus Curse.

00:26:24.125 --> 00:26:26.877
Correct, correct. Come, come.

00:26:27.211 --> 00:26:28.754
Particularly nasty.

00:26:31.757 --> 00:26:33.592
The torture curse.

00:26:34.593 --> 00:26:36.012
Crucio!

00:26:49.442 --> 00:26:53.404
Stop it! Can't you see
it's bothering him? Stop it!

00:27:05.124 --> 00:27:07.293
Um....

00:27:10.921 --> 00:27:14.925
Perhaps you could give us the last
Unforgivable Curse, Miss Granger.

00:27:17.261 --> 00:27:18.471
No?

00:27:19.930 --> 00:27:22.058
Avada Kedavra!

00:27:25.811 --> 00:27:27.438
The Killing Curse.

00:27:28.481 --> 00:27:31.567
Only one person is known
to have survived it...

00:27:32.276 --> 00:27:34.487
...and he's sitting in this room.

00:28:06.227 --> 00:28:07.937
RON:
Brilliant, isn't he?

00:28:08.104 --> 00:28:12.191
Completely demented, of course, and
terrifying to be in the same room with...

00:28:12.358 --> 00:28:15.486
...but he's really been there, you know?
He's looked evil in the eye.

00:28:15.569 --> 00:28:18.322
There's a reason those curses
are unforgivable.

00:28:18.489 --> 00:28:22.535
To perform them in a classroom....
I mean, did you see Neville's face?

00:28:25.538 --> 00:28:26.872
Neville?

00:28:27.123 --> 00:28:28.541
Son?

00:28:28.874 --> 00:28:30.543
You all right?

00:28:31.544 --> 00:28:34.880
Come on. We'll have a cup of tea.
I want to show you something.

00:28:49.520 --> 00:28:51.522
GIRL:
We're gonna be late!

00:29:04.994 --> 00:29:07.413
Come on, Cedric. Put it in!

00:29:22.928 --> 00:29:25.514
Eternal glory. Be brilliant, wouldn't it?

00:29:25.598 --> 00:29:28.309
Three years from now,
when we're old enough to be chosen.

00:29:28.559 --> 00:29:30.060
Yeah, rather you than me.

00:29:30.269 --> 00:29:32.188
FRED AND GEORGE:
Yes!

00:29:34.440 --> 00:29:36.317
Thank you, thank you.

00:29:36.567 --> 00:29:39.528
-Well, lads, we've done it.
-Cooked it up just this morning.

00:29:39.612 --> 00:29:41.780
It's not going to work.

00:29:43.032 --> 00:29:45.534
-Oh, yeah?
-And why is that, Granger?

00:29:45.618 --> 00:29:48.621
You see this? This is an Age Line.

00:29:48.787 --> 00:29:50.623
Dumbledore drew it himself.

00:29:50.706 --> 00:29:52.291
So?

00:29:53.792 --> 00:29:57.546
So a genius like Dumbledore
couldn't possibly be fooled...

00:29:57.630 --> 00:30:00.633
...by a dodge as pathetically dimwitted
as an Aging Potion.

00:30:00.716 --> 00:30:05.054
-But that's why it's so brilliant.
-Because it's so pathetically dimwitted.

00:30:06.722 --> 00:30:08.724
-Ready, Fred?
-Ready, George.

00:30:08.974 --> 00:30:10.726
BOTH:
Bottoms up.

00:30:14.230 --> 00:30:16.106
-Yes!
-Yes!

00:30:16.982 --> 00:30:18.609
Yeah!

00:30:19.652 --> 00:30:21.320
Yes!

00:30:21.654 --> 00:30:23.239
Ready?

00:30:26.617 --> 00:30:28.661
FRED AND GEORGE:
Yes!

00:30:37.127 --> 00:30:39.129
-You said!
-You said!

00:30:40.130 --> 00:30:43.592
-Oh, right, you want a piece of me?!
-I'll tear your ears off!

00:30:43.676 --> 00:30:46.262
-Now you're making me laugh.
-Take this! Come on!

00:30:46.470 --> 00:30:47.763
[CHANTING]
Fight! Fight! Fight!

00:30:52.893 --> 00:30:54.687
FRED:
We're "old school," eh?

00:30:54.770 --> 00:30:57.273
GEORGE:
Yeah, but you look older!

00:31:28.679 --> 00:31:31.307
DUMBLEDORE:
Sit down. Please.

00:31:34.476 --> 00:31:37.354
Now the moment
you've all been waiting for:

00:31:37.730 --> 00:31:39.773
The champion selection.

00:32:11.221 --> 00:32:15.100
The Durmstrang champion
is Viktor Krum.

00:32:30.991 --> 00:32:33.494
The champion for Beauxbatons...

00:32:33.744 --> 00:32:35.704
...is Fleur Delacour.

00:32:46.131 --> 00:32:49.134
The Hogwarts champion,
Cedric Diggory!

00:32:59.228 --> 00:33:03.732
Excellent! We now have
our three champions.

00:33:03.816 --> 00:33:07.903
But in the end,
only one will go down in history.

00:33:08.153 --> 00:33:11.532
Only one will hoist
this chalice of champions...

00:33:11.824 --> 00:33:14.827
...this vessel of victory...

00:33:14.910 --> 00:33:17.162
...the Triwizard Cup!

00:33:47.901 --> 00:33:49.695
Harry Potter.

00:33:51.822 --> 00:33:53.323
Harry Potter?

00:33:57.828 --> 00:33:59.872
No. No.

00:34:00.456 --> 00:34:01.832
Harry Potter!

00:34:02.207 --> 00:34:03.792
Go on, Harry.

00:34:03.876 --> 00:34:05.711
Harry, for goodness sake.

00:34:37.075 --> 00:34:38.327
BOY 1:
He's a cheat!

00:34:38.911 --> 00:34:41.371
BOY 2:
He's not even 17 yet!

00:34:56.345 --> 00:34:58.388
[INSTRUMENTS WHIRRING
AND CLICKING]

00:35:09.274 --> 00:35:12.152
MAXIME: It's wrong, I tell you!
MOODY: You French tart.

00:35:12.402 --> 00:35:14.154
Everything is a conspiracy theory!

00:35:14.404 --> 00:35:15.781
DUMBLEDORE:
Quiet! I can't think!

00:35:15.948 --> 00:35:18.033
-Everything is a conspiracy theory!
MAXIME: I protest.

00:35:18.283 --> 00:35:19.409
DUMBLEDORE: Harry.
-I protest!

00:35:19.660 --> 00:35:21.537
Did you put your name
in the Goblet of Fire?

00:35:21.745 --> 00:35:23.872
-No, sir.
-Did you ask one of the older students...

00:35:23.956 --> 00:35:25.290
-...to do it for you?
-No, sir.

00:35:25.541 --> 00:35:28.418
-You're absolutely sure?
-Yes. Yes, sir.

00:35:28.919 --> 00:35:31.004
-But of course he is lying.
MOODY: The hell he is!

00:35:31.171 --> 00:35:33.757
The Goblet of Fire is an exceptionally
powerful magical object.

00:35:33.924 --> 00:35:36.969
Only an exceptionally powerful
Confundus Charm could've hoodwinked it.

00:35:37.052 --> 00:35:39.054
Magic way beyond the talents
of a fourth year.

00:35:39.304 --> 00:35:42.266
You seem to have given this
a fair bit of thought, Mad-Eye.

00:35:42.432 --> 00:35:45.686
It was once my job to think
as dark wizards do, Karkaroff...

00:35:45.936 --> 00:35:47.312
...perhaps you remember.

00:35:47.563 --> 00:35:49.982
DUMBLEDORE:
This doesn't help, Alastor.

00:35:50.691 --> 00:35:52.985
Leave this to you, Barty.

00:35:54.319 --> 00:35:56.572
The rules are absolute.

00:35:57.823 --> 00:36:01.451
The Goblet of Fire constitutes
a binding magical contract.

00:36:02.995 --> 00:36:05.163
Mr. Potter has no choice.

00:36:05.998 --> 00:36:08.208
He is, as of tonight...

00:36:10.085 --> 00:36:12.087
...a Triwizard champion.

00:36:40.032 --> 00:36:42.200
McGONAGALL:
This can't go on, Albus.

00:36:42.618 --> 00:36:45.370
First the Dark Mark. Now this?

00:36:45.621 --> 00:36:47.623
What do you suggest, Minerva?

00:36:48.832 --> 00:36:50.876
Put an end to it.

00:36:51.251 --> 00:36:53.253
Don't let Potter compete.

00:36:53.462 --> 00:36:55.964
You heard Barty. The rules are clear.

00:36:56.048 --> 00:36:58.967
Well, the devil with Barty
and his rules.

00:36:59.051 --> 00:37:01.511
And since when did you
accommodate the Ministry?

00:37:01.762 --> 00:37:05.766
Headmaster, I, too, find it difficult
to believe this mere coincidence.

00:37:06.016 --> 00:37:09.895
However, if we are to truly discover
the meaning of these events...

00:37:10.062 --> 00:37:13.523
...perhaps we should,
for the time being...

00:37:14.483 --> 00:37:16.777
...let them unfold.

00:37:17.027 --> 00:37:19.071
What--? Do nothing?

00:37:19.154 --> 00:37:21.031
Offer him up as bait?

00:37:22.032 --> 00:37:24.785
Potter is a boy, not a piece of meat.

00:37:25.661 --> 00:37:28.288
I agree. With Severus.

00:37:29.039 --> 00:37:33.001
-Alastor, keep an eye on Harry, will you?
-I can do that.

00:37:33.085 --> 00:37:37.923
Don't let him know, though.
He must be anxious enough as it is...

00:37:38.423 --> 00:37:41.093
...knowing what lies ahead.

00:37:41.426 --> 00:37:44.096
Then again, we all are.

00:37:58.944 --> 00:38:00.696
How did you do it?

00:38:02.114 --> 00:38:04.825
Never mind. Doesn't matter.

00:38:05.075 --> 00:38:06.952
Might've let
your best friend know, though.

00:38:07.119 --> 00:38:10.205
-Let you know what?
-You know bloody well what.

00:38:10.455 --> 00:38:12.916
I didn't ask for this to happen, Ron.

00:38:13.208 --> 00:38:14.960
Okay?

00:38:15.127 --> 00:38:17.587
-You're being stupid.
-Yeah, that's me.

00:38:17.796 --> 00:38:21.216
Ron Weasley,
Harry Potter's stupid friend.

00:38:25.095 --> 00:38:27.097
I didn't put my name in that cup.

00:38:27.347 --> 00:38:31.143
I don't want eternal glory.
I just wanna be....

00:38:33.103 --> 00:38:35.355
Look, I don't know
what happened tonight...

00:38:35.605 --> 00:38:37.441
...and I don't know why.

00:38:37.607 --> 00:38:38.942
It just did.

00:38:39.735 --> 00:38:41.236
Okay?

00:38:50.162 --> 00:38:51.955
Piss off.

00:39:06.970 --> 00:39:09.264
What a charismatic quartet.

00:39:10.640 --> 00:39:12.225
Hello.

00:39:13.185 --> 00:39:15.771
I'm Rita Skeeter.

00:39:16.229 --> 00:39:18.857
I write for the Daily Prophet.

00:39:19.357 --> 00:39:24.196
But of course you know that, don't you?
It's you we don't know.

00:39:24.654 --> 00:39:26.406
You're the juicy news.

00:39:26.656 --> 00:39:30.911
What quirks lurk
beneath those rosy cheeks?

00:39:31.161 --> 00:39:34.498
What mysteries do the muscles mask?

00:39:34.664 --> 00:39:38.001
Does courage lie beneath those curls?

00:39:38.168 --> 00:39:41.213
In short, what makes a champion tick?

00:39:41.630 --> 00:39:46.009
"Me, Myself & I" want to know.
Not to mention my rabid readers.

00:39:46.176 --> 00:39:48.553
So who's feeling up to sharing?

00:39:48.804 --> 00:39:50.931
Hm?

00:39:51.932 --> 00:39:54.434
Shall we start with the youngest?
Lovely.

00:40:06.822 --> 00:40:08.573
This is cozy.

00:40:09.241 --> 00:40:10.909
It's a broom cupboard.

00:40:11.243 --> 00:40:13.453
You should feel right at home, then.

00:40:13.703 --> 00:40:16.456
Don't mind if I use
a Quick-Quotes Quill, do you?

00:40:16.665 --> 00:40:18.250
Oh, no.

00:40:18.583 --> 00:40:20.544
So tell me, Harry.

00:40:20.710 --> 00:40:23.672
Here you sit, a mere boy of 12--

00:40:23.839 --> 00:40:25.257
I'm 14. Sorry.

00:40:25.465 --> 00:40:28.426
--about to compete
against three students...

00:40:28.593 --> 00:40:31.972
...not only vastly more
emotionally mature than yourself...

00:40:32.222 --> 00:40:34.683
...but who have mastered spells
that you wouldn't attempt...

00:40:34.850 --> 00:40:37.269
...in your dizziest daydreams.

00:40:37.686 --> 00:40:39.729
Concerned?

00:40:40.438 --> 00:40:43.733
I-- I don't know.
I haven't really thought about it.

00:40:43.942 --> 00:40:45.735
RITA:
Just ignore the quill.

00:40:46.278 --> 00:40:48.738
Then, of course,
you're no ordinary boy of 12, are you?

00:40:48.989 --> 00:40:51.491
-Fourteen.
-Your story's legend.

00:40:52.284 --> 00:40:54.369
Do you think it was
the trauma of your past...

00:40:54.619 --> 00:40:57.873
...that made you so keen to enter
such a dangerous tournament?

00:40:58.123 --> 00:40:59.749
No, I didn't enter.

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:01.501
Of course you didn't.

00:41:03.879 --> 00:41:05.380
Everyone loves a rebel, Harry.

00:41:07.757 --> 00:41:09.301
Scratch that last.

00:41:10.135 --> 00:41:12.762
Speaking of your parents,
were they alive...

00:41:12.971 --> 00:41:14.306
...how do you think they'd feel?

00:41:14.389 --> 00:41:16.224
Proud? Or concerned...

00:41:16.308 --> 00:41:20.228
...that your attitude shows, at best,
a pathological need for attention...

00:41:20.312 --> 00:41:23.023
...at worst, a psychotic death wish?

00:41:24.024 --> 00:41:29.154
Hey, my eyes aren't
"glistening with the ghosts of my past."

00:42:01.353 --> 00:42:03.647
SIRIUS:
Harry, I couldn't risk sending Hedwig.

00:42:03.813 --> 00:42:07.192
Since the World Cup, the Ministry's
been intercepting more and more owls...

00:42:07.359 --> 00:42:09.444
...and she's too easily recognized.

00:42:09.694 --> 00:42:12.530
We need to talk, Harry, face-to-face.

00:42:12.697 --> 00:42:16.952
Meet me in the Gryffindor common room,
1:00 this Saturday night.

00:42:17.160 --> 00:42:18.828
And make sure you're alone.

00:42:19.079 --> 00:42:20.455
Sirius.

00:42:20.705 --> 00:42:22.290
-P.S.:
-Aah!

00:42:22.374 --> 00:42:24.209
The bird bites.

00:42:25.210 --> 00:42:26.211
Aah.

00:42:34.427 --> 00:42:35.971
Sirius?

00:42:52.821 --> 00:42:54.698
RITA:
Harry Potter, age 12...

00:42:54.864 --> 00:42:57.867
...suspect entrant
in the Triwizard Tournament.

00:42:58.076 --> 00:43:00.578
His eyes swimming
with the ghosts of his past...

00:43:00.745 --> 00:43:02.414
...and choking back tears-- Aah!

00:43:17.846 --> 00:43:20.432
Sirius. How--?

00:43:20.515 --> 00:43:23.143
I don't have much time,
so let me get straight to it.

00:43:23.393 --> 00:43:26.271
Did you or did you not put your name
into the Goblet of Fire?

00:43:26.438 --> 00:43:27.856
-No!
-Shh.

00:43:28.440 --> 00:43:29.649
I had to ask.

00:43:29.899 --> 00:43:34.654
Now, tell me about this dream of yours.
You mentioned Wormtail and Voldemort.

00:43:34.863 --> 00:43:37.365
But who was the third man in the room?

00:43:37.449 --> 00:43:39.909
-I don't know.
-You didn't hear a name?

00:43:40.785 --> 00:43:42.412
No.

00:43:43.288 --> 00:43:46.916
Voldemort was giving him a job to do.
Something important.

00:43:47.167 --> 00:43:48.460
And what was that?

00:43:50.545 --> 00:43:52.297
He wanted...

00:43:52.464 --> 00:43:54.132
...me.

00:43:54.549 --> 00:43:58.928
I don't know why. But he was
gonna use this man to get to me.

00:44:00.305 --> 00:44:02.432
But, I mean, it was only a dream, right?

00:44:02.807 --> 00:44:04.434
Yes.

00:44:04.517 --> 00:44:06.186
It's just a dream.

00:44:06.895 --> 00:44:08.396
Look, Harry.

00:44:08.480 --> 00:44:11.941
The Death Eaters at the World Cup,
your name rising from that goblet...

00:44:12.192 --> 00:44:16.196
...these are not just coincidences.
Hogwarts isn't safe anymore.

00:44:16.446 --> 00:44:17.405
What are you saying?

00:44:17.489 --> 00:44:21.785
I'm saying the devils are inside
the walls. Igor Karkaroff?

00:44:21.951 --> 00:44:26.414
He was a Death Eater. And no one,
no one stops being a Death Eater.

00:44:26.498 --> 00:44:28.958
Then there's Barty Crouch.
Heart of stone.

00:44:29.167 --> 00:44:30.543
Sent his own son to Azkaban.

00:44:36.716 --> 00:44:38.843
You think one of them
put my name in the goblet?

00:44:39.094 --> 00:44:41.429
I haven't a clue who put your name
in that goblet...

00:44:41.513 --> 00:44:45.517
...but whoever did is no friend to you.
People die in this tournament.

00:44:45.600 --> 00:44:49.104
-I'm not ready for this, Sirius.
-You don't have a choice.

00:44:52.607 --> 00:44:55.110
-Someone's coming.
-Keep your friends close, Harry.

00:44:58.488 --> 00:45:00.448
-Who were you talking to?
-What?

00:45:00.532 --> 00:45:02.951
-Who says I was talking to anyone?
-I heard voices.

00:45:03.326 --> 00:45:07.330
Maybe you're imagining things.
Wouldn't be the first time.

00:45:07.747 --> 00:45:11.126
You're probably just practicing
for your next interview, I expect.

00:45:37.026 --> 00:45:38.611
NEVILLE:
Amazing.

00:45:40.572 --> 00:45:43.908
-Amazing!
-Neville. You're doing it again.

00:45:44.159 --> 00:45:46.411
Oh, right, sorry.

00:45:47.245 --> 00:45:50.248
"Magical Water Plants
of the Highland Lochs"?

00:45:50.415 --> 00:45:53.585
Moody gave it to me.
That day we had tea.

00:45:55.044 --> 00:45:56.671
It's already been through enough people.

00:45:56.921 --> 00:45:59.048
Why don't you just go
and talk to him yourself?

00:46:00.592 --> 00:46:02.802
Ron, this is your problem, not mine.

00:46:03.011 --> 00:46:04.596
What do you want me to say again?

00:46:04.762 --> 00:46:06.598
You do it. Go.

00:46:09.601 --> 00:46:13.605
Ronald would like me to tell you
that Seamus told him...

00:46:14.314 --> 00:46:17.817
...that Dean was told by Parvati
that Hagrid's looking for you.

00:46:18.067 --> 00:46:20.528
Is that right? Well, you--

00:46:20.612 --> 00:46:21.654
What?

00:46:22.614 --> 00:46:24.282
Uh....

00:46:26.784 --> 00:46:29.704
-Are you sure you won't do this?
-You do it.

00:46:32.624 --> 00:46:35.627
Dean was told by Parvati that....

00:46:36.711 --> 00:46:38.963
Please don't ask me to say it again.

00:46:39.464 --> 00:46:40.798
Hagrid's looking for you.

00:46:41.424 --> 00:46:44.469
-Well, you can tell Ronald--
-I'm not an owl!

00:46:54.854 --> 00:46:57.357
HAGRID: Did you bring
your father's cloak, like I asked you?

00:46:57.607 --> 00:46:59.943
HARRY: Yeah, I brought the cloak.
Hagrid, where are we going?

00:47:00.109 --> 00:47:01.569
You'll see soon enough.

00:47:01.653 --> 00:47:03.863
Now pay attention, this is important.

00:47:05.657 --> 00:47:07.075
What's with the flower?

00:47:08.117 --> 00:47:10.662
Hagrid, have you combed your hair?

00:47:10.995 --> 00:47:12.664
As a matter of fact, I have.

00:47:13.122 --> 00:47:16.084
You might like to try the same thing
now and again.

00:47:24.676 --> 00:47:26.010
MAXIME:
Hagrid?

00:47:29.889 --> 00:47:31.724
The cloak! Put the cloak on!

00:47:38.481 --> 00:47:41.734
-Bonsoir, Olympe.
-Oh, Hagrid.

00:47:41.901 --> 00:47:45.697
I thought perhaps you weren't coming.
I thought perhaps...

00:47:45.780 --> 00:47:48.616
...you had forgotten me.

00:47:48.700 --> 00:47:50.702
Couldn't forget you, Olympe.

00:47:51.369 --> 00:47:53.037
-Ugh.
-What is it you wanted to show me?

00:47:54.747 --> 00:47:58.042
When we spoke earlier,
you sounded so...

00:47:58.418 --> 00:47:59.794
...exhilarated.

00:48:00.545 --> 00:48:03.298
You'll be glad you came. Trust me.

00:48:13.808 --> 00:48:15.727
MAXIME:
Can we get closer?

00:48:23.526 --> 00:48:24.819
Dragons?

00:48:25.069 --> 00:48:26.696
That's the first task?

00:48:26.946 --> 00:48:28.906
-You're joking.
HAGRID: Come on, Harry.

00:48:30.325 --> 00:48:33.328
These are seriously
misunderstood creatures.

00:48:34.454 --> 00:48:35.830
Oh, crikey!

00:48:36.539 --> 00:48:38.583
Although, I have to admit...

00:48:38.750 --> 00:48:41.586
...that Horntail is a right nasty
piece of work.

00:48:41.753 --> 00:48:44.547
Poor Ron nearly fainted
just seeing him, you know.

00:48:45.965 --> 00:48:48.051
-Ron was here?
-Oh, sure.

00:48:48.217 --> 00:48:51.763
His brother Charlie helped
to bring him over from Romania.

00:48:51.846 --> 00:48:53.348
Didn't Ron tell you that?

00:48:55.350 --> 00:48:56.768
No, he didn't.

00:48:57.477 --> 00:48:59.354
He didn't tell me a thing.

00:49:09.238 --> 00:49:12.367
BOY 1: You cheat, Potter.
BOY 2: You stink, Potter.

00:49:13.785 --> 00:49:16.621
-Good luck, Potter.
BOY 3: Potter stinks!

00:49:16.788 --> 00:49:19.374
-Cedric rules.
HARRY: Thanks.

00:49:20.500 --> 00:49:22.126
Like the badge?

00:49:22.752 --> 00:49:24.462
Excuse me.

00:49:28.633 --> 00:49:30.009
BOY 1:
Harry.

00:49:30.760 --> 00:49:32.637
Hey! Read the badge, Potter!

00:49:32.804 --> 00:49:34.263
Can I have a word?

00:49:35.223 --> 00:49:37.016
-All right.
BOY 2: You stink, Potter!

00:49:37.266 --> 00:49:40.269
BOY 3: Potter, you stink!
BOY 4: Harry Potter smells!

00:49:42.814 --> 00:49:45.274
Dragons. That's the first task.

00:49:45.525 --> 00:49:48.736
-They've got one for each of us.
BOY 2: Come on, Ced!

00:49:48.820 --> 00:49:50.822
Are you serious?

00:49:51.656 --> 00:49:54.742
And Fleur and Krum, do they--?

00:49:54.826 --> 00:49:56.869
-Yes.
BOY 2: Come on, Ced, leave him.

00:49:57.036 --> 00:49:58.746
CEDRIC: Right.
BOY 2: He's not worth it.

00:49:58.830 --> 00:50:01.499
BOY 1: Read the badges, Potter!
-Hey, listen. About the badges.

00:50:01.666 --> 00:50:04.669
-I've asked them not to wear them, but--
-Don't worry about it.

00:50:04.836 --> 00:50:07.171
It's not like I try
to blow things up, exactly.

00:50:07.839 --> 00:50:09.382
It just happens a fair bit.

00:50:09.549 --> 00:50:12.677
You have to admit, though,
fire's pretty fascinating.

00:50:12.844 --> 00:50:14.679
You're a right foul git, you know that?

00:50:14.846 --> 00:50:16.931
-You think so?
-I know so.

00:50:17.181 --> 00:50:18.558
Anything else?

00:50:18.808 --> 00:50:22.186
-Yeah. Stay away from me.
-Fine.

00:50:24.647 --> 00:50:28.192
CRABBE: There's Potter. Cheat.
MALFOY: Why so tense, Potter?

00:50:28.860 --> 00:50:31.320
My father and I have a bet, you see.

00:50:31.571 --> 00:50:34.824
I don't think you're gonna last
10 minutes in this tournament.

00:50:37.285 --> 00:50:40.163
He disagrees.
He thinks you won't last five.

00:50:40.329 --> 00:50:43.541
I don't give a damn
what your father thinks, Malfoy.

00:50:44.542 --> 00:50:48.546
He's vile and cruel.
And you're just pathetic.

00:50:49.464 --> 00:50:51.883
-Pathetic?
-Oh, no, you don't, sonny!

00:50:52.091 --> 00:50:53.593
Aah!

00:50:54.093 --> 00:50:56.971
MOODY: I'll teach you to curse someone
when their back is turned!

00:50:57.221 --> 00:51:00.975
You stinking, cowardly, scummy...

00:51:01.225 --> 00:51:02.894
-Professor Moody!
-...back-shooting--

00:51:03.102 --> 00:51:05.980
-What are you doing?
-Teaching.

00:51:06.981 --> 00:51:10.693
-Is that a--? Is that a student?
-Technically, it's a ferret.

00:51:10.860 --> 00:51:12.987
Oh! Ah!

00:51:16.908 --> 00:51:18.868
Stand still! Stand still!

00:51:29.879 --> 00:51:31.923
-My father will hear about this!
-Is that a threat?

00:51:32.089 --> 00:51:34.008
-Professor Moody!
-Is that a threat?

00:51:34.217 --> 00:51:36.093
Professor!

00:51:36.260 --> 00:51:39.847
I could tell you stories about your father
that would curl even your greasy hair!

00:51:39.931 --> 00:51:42.767
-Alastor! Alastor.
-It doesn't end here!

00:51:42.934 --> 00:51:46.771
We never use transfiguration
as a punishment!

00:51:46.938 --> 00:51:48.981
Surely Dumbledore told you that.

00:51:49.649 --> 00:51:53.986
-He might've mentioned it.
-Well, you will do well to remember it.

00:51:55.112 --> 00:51:56.656
Away!

00:51:59.784 --> 00:52:01.953
You. Come with me.

00:52:37.071 --> 00:52:39.198
That's a Foe-Glass.

00:52:39.991 --> 00:52:41.993
Lets me keep an eye on my enemies.

00:52:42.577 --> 00:52:46.998
If I can see the whites of their eyes,
they're standing right behind me.

00:52:51.043 --> 00:52:53.588
Wouldn't even bother telling you
what's in there.

00:52:53.838 --> 00:52:55.840
You wouldn't believe it if I did.

00:52:56.007 --> 00:52:57.842
Now...

00:52:59.427 --> 00:53:02.221
...what are you going to do
about your dragon?

00:53:02.430 --> 00:53:05.016
Oh, um....

00:53:06.100 --> 00:53:08.477
Well, you know, I just thought I'd....

00:53:10.021 --> 00:53:11.439
Sit.

00:53:15.067 --> 00:53:16.485
Listen to me, Potter.

00:53:17.486 --> 00:53:18.738
Your pal Diggory?

00:53:18.988 --> 00:53:23.242
By your age, he could turn a whistle into
a watch and have it sing you the time.

00:53:24.493 --> 00:53:25.828
Miss Delacour?

00:53:26.078 --> 00:53:28.998
She's as much a fairy princess as I am.

00:53:29.373 --> 00:53:32.960
As for Krum, his head
may be filled with sawdust...

00:53:33.044 --> 00:53:35.254
...but Karkaroff's is not.

00:53:35.463 --> 00:53:37.256
They'll have a strategy.

00:53:37.465 --> 00:53:41.010
And you can bet that it will
play to Krum's strengths.

00:53:45.848 --> 00:53:47.266
Come on, Potter.

00:53:47.516 --> 00:53:49.644
What are your strengths?

00:53:49.852 --> 00:53:51.020
Um....

00:53:51.103 --> 00:53:52.521
I don't know.

00:53:52.772 --> 00:53:55.524
Well, I can fly.
I mean, I'm a fair flyer. But I....

00:53:55.733 --> 00:53:59.779
-Better than fair, the way I heard it.
-But I'm not allowed a broom.

00:54:00.029 --> 00:54:03.532
You're allowed a wand.

00:54:10.039 --> 00:54:11.374
FRED:
Bets! Place your bets!

00:54:11.540 --> 00:54:13.793
GEORGE:
Bets taken! Bets taken here!

00:54:14.043 --> 00:54:16.921
Step up, folks! Who fancies a flutter
in today's bloodbath?

00:54:17.088 --> 00:54:19.924
Smart money's on Krum to survive!
Any bets?

00:54:20.091 --> 00:54:21.550
Yes, sir?

00:54:22.051 --> 00:54:24.553
Ten-to-1 for Fleur. There you go.
Thank you very much.

00:54:25.096 --> 00:54:27.098
DUMBLEDORE:
Your attention, please.

00:54:27.264 --> 00:54:30.017
This is a great day for all of us.

00:54:33.312 --> 00:54:37.566
Each of the three tasks involves
very considerable danger.

00:54:37.817 --> 00:54:40.403
-Please keep your seats at all times.
VOICE: Psst.

00:54:40.569 --> 00:54:43.322
This will minimize any risks
you may be exposed to.

00:54:43.531 --> 00:54:47.034
-Harry? Is that you?
-Yeah.

00:54:47.118 --> 00:54:48.911
I'm sure we all wish our champions...

00:54:49.078 --> 00:54:52.123
-How are you feeling? Okay?
-...the greatest of luck.

00:54:54.333 --> 00:54:57.837
The key is to concentrate.
After that, you just have to--

00:54:58.087 --> 00:54:59.839
Battle a dragon.

00:55:04.135 --> 00:55:06.554
RITA:
Young love.

00:55:06.804 --> 00:55:08.556
Oh, how...

00:55:11.100 --> 00:55:12.226
...stirring.

00:55:15.104 --> 00:55:18.149
If everything goes unfortunately today...

00:55:18.232 --> 00:55:21.110
...you two may even
make the front page.

00:55:21.193 --> 00:55:23.446
You have no business here.

00:55:23.612 --> 00:55:25.614
This tent is for champions...

00:55:26.115 --> 00:55:27.742
...and friends.

00:55:30.494 --> 00:55:34.749
No matter. We've got what we wanted.

00:55:37.877 --> 00:55:40.629
Good day, champions.
Gather round, please.

00:55:40.880 --> 00:55:45.092
Now, you've waited, you've wondered,
and at last the moment has arrived.

00:55:45.176 --> 00:55:48.387
A moment only four of you
can fully appreciate.

00:55:48.596 --> 00:55:50.598
What are you doing here, Miss Granger?

00:55:50.765 --> 00:55:53.642
Oh, um, sorry, I'll just go.

00:55:53.893 --> 00:55:55.352
Barty, the bag.

00:55:55.895 --> 00:55:58.105
Champions, in a circle around me.

00:55:58.189 --> 00:56:01.275
Miss Delacour, over here. Mr. Krum.

00:56:01.525 --> 00:56:05.404
And, Potter, Mr. Potter, over here.
That's right. Now...

00:56:05.613 --> 00:56:08.157
...Miss Delacour, if you will.

00:56:12.203 --> 00:56:13.788
CROUCH:
The Welsh Green.

00:56:18.375 --> 00:56:19.668
Mr. Krum.

00:56:22.671 --> 00:56:26.050
The Chinese Fireball. Ooh.

00:56:31.180 --> 00:56:33.432
The Swedish Short-Snout.

00:56:34.058 --> 00:56:36.060
-Which leaves....
-The Horntail.

00:56:36.227 --> 00:56:38.312
-What's that, boy?
-Nothing.

00:56:41.816 --> 00:56:44.235
CROUCH:
The Hungarian Horntail.

00:56:46.320 --> 00:56:49.448
These represent four
very real dragons...

00:56:49.698 --> 00:56:52.701
...each of which has been given
a golden egg to protect.

00:56:52.952 --> 00:56:55.329
Your objective is simple:

00:56:55.579 --> 00:56:57.164
Collect the egg.

00:56:57.248 --> 00:57:00.251
This you must do,
for each egg contains a clue...

00:57:00.334 --> 00:57:03.963
...without which you cannot hope
to proceed to the next task.

00:57:04.213 --> 00:57:05.339
Any questions?

00:57:06.340 --> 00:57:09.176
Very well. Good luck, champions.

00:57:09.260 --> 00:57:12.096
Mr. Diggory, at the sound of the cannon,
you may--

00:57:20.729 --> 00:57:24.483
CROWD [CHANTING]:
Diggory! Diggory! Diggory!

00:57:36.245 --> 00:57:39.456
DUMBLEDORE: Three of our champions
have now faced their dragons...

00:57:39.623 --> 00:57:43.210
...and so each one of them
will proceed to the next task.

00:57:43.294 --> 00:57:46.881
And now our fourth
and final contestant.

00:57:48.757 --> 00:57:52.303
CROWD [CHANTING]:
Harry! Harry! Harry!

00:58:17.536 --> 00:58:19.121
CROWD:
Oh!

00:58:41.810 --> 00:58:43.062
Aah!

00:58:59.411 --> 00:59:02.373
Your wand, Harry! Your wand!

00:59:02.957 --> 00:59:04.959
Accio Firebolt!

00:59:33.988 --> 00:59:36.198
-Yeah! Woo-hoo!
-Yes!

00:59:39.368 --> 00:59:40.577
Ooh.

00:59:45.082 --> 00:59:46.417
Oh, my God.

00:59:56.135 --> 00:59:59.430
-Yeah! Whoo!
-Yeah! Well done, dragon!

01:00:56.945 --> 01:00:58.572
Aah!

01:02:31.540 --> 01:02:33.584
Yes! Yes!

01:02:56.690 --> 01:02:59.526
-Yes, Harry!
-Knew you wouldn't die. Lose a leg.

01:02:59.610 --> 01:03:01.612
-Or an arm.
-Pack it in altogether?

01:03:01.695 --> 01:03:03.614
BOTH:
Never!

01:03:05.616 --> 01:03:06.950
SEAMUS:
Shush!

01:03:07.576 --> 01:03:10.078
Go on, Harry. What's the clue?

01:03:11.079 --> 01:03:13.957
-Who wants me to open it?
ALL: Yes!

01:03:14.708 --> 01:03:17.336
-Do you want me to open it?
-Yes!

01:03:28.597 --> 01:03:30.849
What the bloody hell was that?

01:03:34.978 --> 01:03:37.689
All right, everyone!
Go back to your knitting.

01:03:37.856 --> 01:03:41.985
This is gonna be uncomfortable enough
without all you nosy sods listening in.

01:03:45.113 --> 01:03:49.076
I reckon you have to be barking mad to
put your own name in the Goblet of Fire.

01:03:49.618 --> 01:03:52.246
Caught on, have you?
Took you long enough.

01:03:53.372 --> 01:03:55.499
I wasn't the only one
who thought you'd done it.

01:03:55.666 --> 01:03:57.834
Everyone was saying it
behind your back.

01:04:00.087 --> 01:04:03.382
Brilliant.
That makes me feel loads better.

01:04:04.258 --> 01:04:07.636
-Least I warned you about the dragons.
-Hagrid warned me about the dragons.

01:04:07.719 --> 01:04:09.346
No, no, no, I did.

01:04:09.513 --> 01:04:12.599
No, don't you remember?
I told Hermione to tell you...

01:04:12.683 --> 01:04:16.687
...that Seamus told me that Parvati
told Dean that Hagrid was looking for you.

01:04:16.853 --> 01:04:20.774
Seamus never actually told me anything,
so it was really me all along.

01:04:21.775 --> 01:04:24.778
I thought we'd be all right, you know...

01:04:25.028 --> 01:04:27.030
...after you'd figured that out.

01:04:27.531 --> 01:04:30.117
Who--? Who could possibly
figure that out?

01:04:30.701 --> 01:04:32.160
That's completely mental.

01:04:32.411 --> 01:04:35.497
Yeah. Isn't it?

01:04:35.664 --> 01:04:37.708
I suppose I was a bit distraught.

01:04:40.168 --> 01:04:41.878
Boys.

01:05:06.445 --> 01:05:07.738
BOTH:
Hi, Harry.

01:05:11.533 --> 01:05:14.077
Cho, Harry's looking at you.

01:05:17.956 --> 01:05:19.750
CHO:
Shush.

01:05:20.459 --> 01:05:21.752
HERMIONE:
Look at this!

01:05:23.754 --> 01:05:26.214
I can't believe it! She's done it again.

01:05:27.341 --> 01:05:29.593
"Miss Granger,
a plain but ambitious girl...

01:05:29.760 --> 01:05:32.554
...seems to be developing a taste
for famous wizards.

01:05:32.721 --> 01:05:34.848
Her latest prey, sources report...

01:05:35.098 --> 01:05:38.769
...is none other than the
Bulgarian bonbon, Viktor Krum.

01:05:38.977 --> 01:05:42.856
No word yet on how Harry Potter's
taking this latest emotional blow."

01:05:44.358 --> 01:05:45.692
Parcel for you, Mr. Weasley.

01:05:45.776 --> 01:05:47.861
Oh, thank you, Nigel.

01:05:52.783 --> 01:05:55.619
Not now, Nigel. Later.

01:05:57.454 --> 01:05:58.872
Go on.

01:06:04.252 --> 01:06:07.005
I told him I'd get him Harry's autograph.

01:06:09.257 --> 01:06:10.967
Oh, look, Mum's sent me something.

01:06:19.142 --> 01:06:20.894
Mum sent me a dress.

01:06:21.144 --> 01:06:24.898
Well, it does match your eyes.
Is there a bonnet? Aha.

01:06:25.482 --> 01:06:27.275
Nose down, Harry.

01:06:27.818 --> 01:06:31.780
-Ginny, these must be for you.
-I'm not wearing that, it's ghastly.

01:06:33.532 --> 01:06:35.283
What are you on about?

01:06:35.534 --> 01:06:37.494
They're not for Ginny.

01:06:37.661 --> 01:06:38.870
They're for you.

01:06:39.913 --> 01:06:43.834
-Dress robes.
-Dress robes? For what?

01:06:44.918 --> 01:06:48.505
McGONAGALL:
The Yule Ball has been a tradition...

01:06:50.048 --> 01:06:52.801
...of the Triwizard Tournament...

01:06:53.427 --> 01:06:55.512
...since its inception.

01:06:56.054 --> 01:06:59.933
On Christmas Eve night,
we and our guests...

01:07:00.183 --> 01:07:01.852
...gather in the Great Hall...

01:07:01.935 --> 01:07:06.022
...for a night of well-mannered frivolity.

01:07:07.691 --> 01:07:09.860
As representatives of the host school...

01:07:09.943 --> 01:07:15.031
...I expect each and every one of you
to put your best foot forward.

01:07:15.449 --> 01:07:18.034
And I mean this literally, because...

01:07:18.201 --> 01:07:22.831
...the Yule Ball is, first and foremost...

01:07:23.582 --> 01:07:24.958
...a dance.

01:07:29.296 --> 01:07:31.047
Silence!

01:07:31.298 --> 01:07:34.301
The house of Godric Gryffindor
has commanded the respect...

01:07:34.468 --> 01:07:37.053
...of the wizard world
for nearly 10 centuries.

01:07:37.220 --> 01:07:41.349
I will not have you, in the course of a
single evening, besmirching that name...

01:07:41.558 --> 01:07:45.854
...by behaving like a babbling,
bumbling band of baboons.

01:07:46.480 --> 01:07:48.356
Try saying that five times fast, huh?

01:07:48.607 --> 01:07:49.983
McGONAGALL:
Now, to dance...

01:07:50.233 --> 01:07:53.904
...is to let the body breathe.

01:07:54.070 --> 01:07:57.491
Inside every girl,
a secret swan slumbers...

01:07:57.699 --> 01:07:59.910
...longing to burst forth
and take flight.

01:08:00.118 --> 01:08:04.122
Something's about to burst out of Eloise
Midgen, but I don't think it's a swan.

01:08:04.331 --> 01:08:07.501
Inside every boy,
a lordly lion prepared to prance.

01:08:07.709 --> 01:08:09.878
-Mr. Weasley.
-Yes?

01:08:09.961 --> 01:08:12.506
Will you join me, please?

01:08:17.010 --> 01:08:20.639
Now, place your right hand
on my waist.

01:08:20.889 --> 01:08:22.766
-Where?
-My waist.

01:08:23.975 --> 01:08:25.977
And extend your arm.

01:08:26.520 --> 01:08:28.522
Mr. Filch, if you please.

01:08:31.942 --> 01:08:33.610
One, two, three.

01:08:33.777 --> 01:08:37.155
One, two, three. One, two, three.

01:08:39.157 --> 01:08:40.742
HARRY:
Oi!

01:08:40.951 --> 01:08:42.994
Never gonna let him forget this,
are you?

01:08:43.161 --> 01:08:44.412
BOTH:
Never.

01:08:44.621 --> 01:08:45.956
McGONAGALL:
Everybody come together.

01:08:46.122 --> 01:08:48.416
Boys, on your feet!

01:09:11.565 --> 01:09:13.441
Why do they have to travel in packs?

01:09:13.692 --> 01:09:16.194
How are you supposed to get one
on their own to ask them?

01:09:24.077 --> 01:09:27.706
Blimey, Harry. You've slayed dragons.
If you can't get a date, who can?

01:09:27.956 --> 01:09:30.000
I think I'd take the dragon right now.

01:09:36.214 --> 01:09:37.924
I take after my mum.

01:09:38.008 --> 01:09:41.970
Though I didn't know her very well.
She left when I was about 3.

01:09:42.053 --> 01:09:44.014
No, not the maternal sort, her.

01:09:44.180 --> 01:09:47.851
Broke me dad's heart, though.
He was a tiny little fella, my dad.

01:09:48.018 --> 01:09:52.480
I could pick him up at the age of 6 with
one hand and put him up on the dresser.

01:09:52.731 --> 01:09:55.025
He laughed so hard at that.

01:09:57.027 --> 01:09:59.029
Very funny.

01:10:04.993 --> 01:10:08.622
And then he died
just when I started school, so....

01:10:08.872 --> 01:10:11.875
So I sort of had to make
me own way, as it were.

01:10:12.208 --> 01:10:14.377
But enough of me. What about you?

01:10:31.728 --> 01:10:36.858
This is mad. At this rate, we'll be
the only ones in our year without dates.

01:10:39.069 --> 01:10:41.863
Well, us and Neville.

01:10:42.030 --> 01:10:44.658
Yeah, but, then again,
he can take himself.

01:10:45.283 --> 01:10:48.078
It might interest you to know
that Neville's already got someone.

01:10:51.081 --> 01:10:53.041
Now I'm really depressed.

01:10:58.797 --> 01:11:02.092
[WHISPERS] "Get a move on or all
the good ones will have gone."

01:11:04.177 --> 01:11:06.179
Who you going with, then?

01:11:09.057 --> 01:11:10.684
FRED: Oi, Angelina?
[MOUTHS] What?

01:11:10.934 --> 01:11:16.106
[WHISPERS]
Do you wanna go to the ball with me?

01:11:16.439 --> 01:11:18.149
To the ball?

01:11:18.316 --> 01:11:19.901
Yeah, all right.

01:11:23.571 --> 01:11:25.115
Oi, Hermione.

01:11:25.198 --> 01:11:27.033
You're a girl.

01:11:27.117 --> 01:11:28.410
Very well spotted.

01:11:28.576 --> 01:11:30.537
Come with one of us?

01:11:35.125 --> 01:11:38.086
Come on. It's one thing for a bloke
to show up alone.

01:11:38.169 --> 01:11:39.796
For a girl, it's just sad.

01:11:39.963 --> 01:11:43.717
I won't be going alone, because,
believe it or not, someone's asked me!

01:11:50.598 --> 01:11:52.600
And I said yes!

01:11:54.477 --> 01:11:56.062
Bloody hell.

01:11:56.146 --> 01:11:57.981
She's lying, right?

01:11:58.148 --> 01:11:59.190
If you say so.

01:12:00.108 --> 01:12:03.236
RON: Look, we've just gotta
grit our teeth and do it.

01:12:03.486 --> 01:12:05.572
Tonight, when we get back
to the common room...

01:12:05.739 --> 01:12:07.365
...we'll both have partners. Agreed?

01:12:07.615 --> 01:12:09.117
Agreed.

01:12:33.391 --> 01:12:34.517
-Cho!
-Harry!

01:12:37.854 --> 01:12:41.107
Um, watch yourself on the stairs.
It's a bit icy at the top.

01:12:41.191 --> 01:12:42.901
Okay, thanks.

01:12:47.238 --> 01:12:48.281
Cho?

01:12:49.240 --> 01:12:50.909
-Yes?
-Um....

01:12:52.202 --> 01:12:53.661
Well, I just wondered if you--

01:12:55.163 --> 01:12:57.373
I wondered if maybe
you wanted to go to the ball with me.

01:12:59.209 --> 01:13:01.294
Sorry, I didn't catch that.

01:13:02.212 --> 01:13:07.217
I was just wondering if maybe
you wanted to go to the ball with me.

01:13:09.219 --> 01:13:11.221
Oh, um....

01:13:13.223 --> 01:13:14.808
Harry...

01:13:15.058 --> 01:13:17.811
...I'm sorry, but someone's
already asked me.

01:13:18.812 --> 01:13:20.230
And....

01:13:20.939 --> 01:13:24.234
Well, I've said I'll go with him.

01:13:25.819 --> 01:13:28.279
Okay. Yeah. Great.

01:13:29.697 --> 01:13:32.325
Fine. No problem.

01:13:32.700 --> 01:13:34.244
Okay. Good.

01:13:35.829 --> 01:13:37.247
Harry?

01:13:38.039 --> 01:13:39.707
I really am...

01:13:39.958 --> 01:13:41.584
...sorry.

01:13:51.261 --> 01:13:52.846
It's all right, Ron.

01:13:53.096 --> 01:13:56.224
It's okay, Ron. It's all right.
It doesn't matter.

01:13:56.307 --> 01:13:58.268
HARRY:
What happened to you?

01:13:58.476 --> 01:14:00.687
He just asked Fleur Delacour out.

01:14:00.854 --> 01:14:03.273
-What?
-What did she say?

01:14:03.481 --> 01:14:04.941
No, of course.

01:14:06.359 --> 01:14:09.737
-She said yes?
RON: Don't be silly.

01:14:10.280 --> 01:14:14.617
There she was, walking by.
You know how I like it when they walk.

01:14:15.285 --> 01:14:19.080
I couldn't help it.
It just sort of slipped out.

01:14:19.247 --> 01:14:22.500
Actually, he sort of screamed at her.
It was a bit frightening.

01:14:23.751 --> 01:14:27.338
-And what did you do then?
-What else? I ran for it.

01:14:27.505 --> 01:14:31.301
I'm not cut out for this, Harry.
I don't know what got into me.

01:14:31.384 --> 01:14:32.719
BOTH:
Hi, Harry.

01:14:32.886 --> 01:14:36.014
RON: I always liked looking at them
from behind.

01:14:37.307 --> 01:14:39.893
She's never gonna forgive me, ever.

01:14:40.351 --> 01:14:41.394
Hey!

01:14:58.536 --> 01:15:00.330
RON:
Bloody hell.

01:15:02.415 --> 01:15:04.334
Bloody hell.

01:15:07.795 --> 01:15:09.172
Bloody....

01:15:09.339 --> 01:15:10.381
Oh, bloody....

01:15:14.302 --> 01:15:16.930
What are those? What are those?

01:15:17.138 --> 01:15:20.183
-My dress robes.
-Well, they're all right!

01:15:20.350 --> 01:15:23.269
No lace. No dodgy little collar.

01:15:23.353 --> 01:15:25.355
Well, I expect yours are more traditional.

01:15:25.438 --> 01:15:30.360
Traditional?! They're ancient!
I look like my Great Aunt Tessie!

01:15:32.820 --> 01:15:35.949
I smell like my Great Aunt Tessie.

01:15:40.703 --> 01:15:42.455
Murder me, Harry.

01:15:43.957 --> 01:15:45.416
Leave it alone!

01:15:46.376 --> 01:15:49.837
Poor kid. I bet she's alone in her room,
crying her eyes out.

01:15:50.088 --> 01:15:52.465
-Who?
-Hermione, of course.

01:15:52.715 --> 01:15:56.302
Come on, Harry, why do you think she
wouldn't tell us who she's coming with?

01:15:56.386 --> 01:15:58.596
Because we'd take the mickey out of her
if she did.

01:15:58.846 --> 01:16:03.977
Nobody asked her. Would've taken her
myself if she wasn't so bloody proud.

01:16:04.852 --> 01:16:06.312
BOTH:
Hello, boys.

01:16:06.396 --> 01:16:08.398
Don't you look...

01:16:08.856 --> 01:16:10.108
...dashing.

01:16:10.608 --> 01:16:13.820
There you are, Potter.
Are you and Miss Patil ready?

01:16:13.987 --> 01:16:15.822
-Ready, professor?
-To dance.

01:16:15.989 --> 01:16:19.075
It's traditional that the three
champions-- Well, in this case, four.

01:16:19.242 --> 01:16:20.368
--are the first to dance.

01:16:20.493 --> 01:16:23.246
-Surely I told you that.
-No.

01:16:23.413 --> 01:16:25.456
Oh, well, now you know.

01:16:25.623 --> 01:16:27.083
Oh.

01:16:27.458 --> 01:16:31.337
As for you, Mr. Weasley, you may proceed
into the Great Hall with Miss Patil.

01:16:31.421 --> 01:16:33.840
-Oh, there you are.
-Come on, then.

01:16:34.090 --> 01:16:35.508
McGONAGALL:
Come along this way.

01:16:40.430 --> 01:16:42.390
Oh, come on.

01:16:43.141 --> 01:16:44.225
Hi.

01:16:44.392 --> 01:16:47.103
Now, I need you all to line up
in the procession, please.

01:16:47.270 --> 01:16:48.604
Oh, you are very late.

01:16:50.857 --> 01:16:53.401
This way. This way. Come along.

01:16:54.902 --> 01:16:57.280
She looks beautiful!

01:16:57.447 --> 01:16:58.906
Yeah, she does.

01:17:46.454 --> 01:17:49.916
Is that Hermione Granger?
With Viktor Krum?

01:17:50.500 --> 01:17:53.169
No. Absolutely not.

01:17:57.840 --> 01:17:59.467
Hi!

01:18:08.184 --> 01:18:10.103
Harry, take my waist.

01:18:10.978 --> 01:18:12.480
-What?
-Now!

01:19:03.614 --> 01:19:04.907
Ooh.

01:19:19.046 --> 01:19:20.756
MAN:
Are you ready?!

01:19:21.549 --> 01:19:23.593
[SINGING]
Move your body like a hairy troll

01:19:24.552 --> 01:19:26.929
Learning to rock and roll

01:19:27.430 --> 01:19:29.932
Spin around like a crazy elf

01:19:30.558 --> 01:19:32.602
Dancing by himself

01:19:32.935 --> 01:19:36.397
Boogie down like a unicorn

01:19:36.564 --> 01:19:38.900
No stopping till the break of dawn

01:19:39.066 --> 01:19:41.903
Put your hands up in the air

01:19:42.069 --> 01:19:44.822
Like an ogre who just don't care

01:19:45.615 --> 01:19:48.326
Can you dance like a Hippogriff?

01:19:50.620 --> 01:19:52.705
Ruddy pumpkinhead, isn't he?

01:19:54.957 --> 01:19:58.461
I don't think it was the books
that had him going to the library.

01:20:00.338 --> 01:20:01.797
May I have your arm?

01:20:01.964 --> 01:20:04.634
Arm. Leg. I'm yours.

01:20:30.660 --> 01:20:32.245
Hot, isn't it?

01:20:32.870 --> 01:20:36.249
Viktor's gone to go and get drinks.
Would you care to join us?

01:20:36.499 --> 01:20:40.086
No, we'd not care to join you and Viktor.

01:20:41.712 --> 01:20:44.131
What's got your wand in a knot?

01:20:44.507 --> 01:20:48.094
He's a Durmstrang.
You're fraternizing with the enemy.

01:20:48.261 --> 01:20:51.764
The enemy?
Who was it wanting his autograph?

01:20:52.640 --> 01:20:54.976
Besides, the whole point
of the tournament...

01:20:55.142 --> 01:20:58.688
...is international
magical cooperation...

01:20:59.272 --> 01:21:00.731
...to make friends.

01:21:01.649 --> 01:21:04.694
I think he's got a bit more
than friendship on his mind.

01:21:14.704 --> 01:21:16.914
Are you going to ask me
to dance or not?

01:21:17.164 --> 01:21:18.666
No.

01:21:26.757 --> 01:21:29.302
-He's using you.
-How dare you?!

01:21:29.510 --> 01:21:33.639
-Besides, I can take care of myself.
-I doubt it. He's way too old.

01:21:33.723 --> 01:21:37.560
-What?! What? That's what you think?
-Yeah, that's what I think.

01:21:37.727 --> 01:21:39.729
You know the solution then, don't you?

01:21:39.895 --> 01:21:41.897
-Go on.
-Next time there's a ball...

01:21:42.064 --> 01:21:45.192
...pluck up the courage and ask me
before somebody else does!

01:21:45.443 --> 01:21:47.528
And not as a last resort.

01:21:47.695 --> 01:21:51.741
Well, that's-- I mean,
that's just completely off the point.

01:21:51.949 --> 01:21:53.326
Harry.

01:21:53.743 --> 01:21:55.036
Where have you been?

01:21:55.202 --> 01:21:57.747
Never mind! Off to bed, both of you.

01:22:00.708 --> 01:22:04.670
-They get scary when they get older.
-Ron, you spoiled everything!

01:22:04.754 --> 01:22:06.714
What's this about?

01:22:10.843 --> 01:22:13.846
SINGER:
No, don't let

01:22:15.765 --> 01:22:19.977
This magic die

01:22:21.771 --> 01:22:24.732
The answer's there

01:23:22.832 --> 01:23:24.917
VOLDEMORT:
Let me see it again.

01:23:26.293 --> 01:23:29.171
Yes, the time is close now.

01:23:33.843 --> 01:23:35.845
Harry, at last!

01:23:37.054 --> 01:23:42.435
Step aside, Wormtail,
so I can give our guest a proper greeting.

01:23:52.945 --> 01:23:54.447
You all right, Harry?

01:23:55.865 --> 01:23:57.700
I just got in.

01:23:58.200 --> 01:23:59.535
Me.

01:24:10.838 --> 01:24:13.966
HERMIONE: Harry, you told me
you'd figured the egg out weeks ago.

01:24:14.216 --> 01:24:18.345
-The task is two days from now.
-Really? I had no idea.

01:24:19.889 --> 01:24:21.807
I suppose Viktor's
already figured it out.

01:24:21.891 --> 01:24:24.852
Wouldn't know. We don't actually
talk about the tournament.

01:24:25.895 --> 01:24:30.608
Actually, we don't really talk at all.
Viktor's more of a physical being.

01:24:34.236 --> 01:24:37.490
I just mean he's not
particularly loquacious.

01:24:37.740 --> 01:24:40.117
-Mm-hm.
-Mostly, he watches me study.

01:24:40.910 --> 01:24:42.995
It's a bit annoying, actually.

01:24:44.497 --> 01:24:47.124
You are trying to figure this egg out,
aren't you?

01:24:47.917 --> 01:24:49.502
What's that supposed to mean?

01:24:50.002 --> 01:24:53.005
It just means these tasks
are designed to test you...

01:24:53.255 --> 01:24:56.383
...in the most brutal way.
They're almost cruel.

01:24:57.635 --> 01:24:59.136
And...

01:25:01.597 --> 01:25:03.390
...I'm scared for you.

01:25:04.391 --> 01:25:06.936
You got by the dragons
mostly on nerve.

01:25:07.645 --> 01:25:10.022
I'm not sure it's going
to be enough this time.

01:25:10.272 --> 01:25:11.941
CEDRIC:
Hey, Potter!

01:25:17.780 --> 01:25:19.156
-Potter!
HARRY: Cedric.

01:25:21.951 --> 01:25:23.619
How--? How are you?

01:25:24.662 --> 01:25:25.955
Spectacular.

01:25:27.623 --> 01:25:29.208
I realize I never really
thanked you properly

01:25:29.250 --> 01:25:31.418
for tipping me off about those dragons.

01:25:31.627 --> 01:25:33.963
Forget it. I'm sure you
would've done the same for me.

01:25:34.171 --> 01:25:35.923
Exactly.

01:25:36.966 --> 01:25:39.385
You know the Prefects' bathroom
on the fifth floor?

01:25:43.305 --> 01:25:45.975
It's not a bad place for a bath.

01:25:48.185 --> 01:25:50.062
Just take your egg...

01:25:50.980 --> 01:25:53.691
...and mull things over
in the hot water.

01:26:28.976 --> 01:26:31.020
I must be out of my mind.

01:26:41.113 --> 01:26:43.365
I'm definitely out of my mind.

01:26:46.035 --> 01:26:49.246
I'd try putting it in the water
if I were you.

01:26:49.496 --> 01:26:51.332
Myrtle!

01:26:51.498 --> 01:26:53.250
Hello, Harry.

01:26:54.043 --> 01:26:57.254
Long time no see.

01:26:57.463 --> 01:26:59.381
Oh.

01:27:01.508 --> 01:27:05.137
I was circling a blocked drain
the other day...

01:27:05.387 --> 01:27:08.891
...and could swear I saw a bit
of Polyjuice Potion.

01:27:09.058 --> 01:27:11.268
Not being a bad boy again,
are you, Harry?

01:27:11.518 --> 01:27:13.228
Polyjuice Potion?

01:27:14.063 --> 01:27:18.067
Kicked the habit. Myrtle, did you say,
"Try putting it in the water"?

01:27:25.032 --> 01:27:26.533
That's what he did.

01:27:27.409 --> 01:27:29.078
The other boy...

01:27:30.496 --> 01:27:32.539
...the handsome one...

01:27:33.916 --> 01:27:35.125
...Cedric.

01:27:38.504 --> 01:27:41.090
Well, go on. Open it.

01:27:49.181 --> 01:27:54.186
WOMAN [SINGING]: Come seek us
Where our voices sound

01:27:54.436 --> 01:27:59.108
We cannot sing
Above the ground

01:27:59.191 --> 01:28:03.570
An hour long you'll have to look

01:28:04.321 --> 01:28:09.118
To recover what we took

01:28:17.167 --> 01:28:18.794
Myrtle...

01:28:20.129 --> 01:28:23.132
...there aren't merpeople
in the Black Lake, are there?

01:28:23.215 --> 01:28:26.135
Oh, very good.

01:28:27.094 --> 01:28:31.348
It took Cedric ages to riddle it out.

01:28:31.974 --> 01:28:35.602
Almost all the bubbles were gone.

01:28:47.865 --> 01:28:49.742
Oh, Harry.

01:28:53.245 --> 01:28:55.247
Harry, tell me again.

01:28:57.124 --> 01:28:59.877
"Come seek us
where our voices sound."

01:29:00.127 --> 01:29:03.213
The Black Lake, that's obvious.

01:29:03.630 --> 01:29:06.091
"An hour long you'll have to look."

01:29:06.175 --> 01:29:09.720
Again, obvious. Though, admittedly,
potentially problematic.

01:29:11.180 --> 01:29:13.015
"Potentially problematic"?

01:29:13.182 --> 01:29:16.268
When's the last time you held your breath
underwater for an hour, Hermione?

01:29:17.019 --> 01:29:21.190
Look, Harry, we can do this.
The three of us can figure it out.

01:29:21.398 --> 01:29:24.026
MOODY:
Hate to break up the skull session.

01:29:24.193 --> 01:29:26.195
Professor McGonagall
wants you in her office.

01:29:26.278 --> 01:29:28.739
Not you, Potter,
just Weasley and Granger.

01:29:28.906 --> 01:29:31.533
But, sir, the second task
is only hours away, and--

01:29:31.742 --> 01:29:34.286
Exactly. Presumably Potter
is well prepared by now...

01:29:34.495 --> 01:29:36.288
...and could do with
a good night's sleep.

01:29:36.538 --> 01:29:39.166
Go. Now!

01:29:49.134 --> 01:29:50.886
Longbottom!

01:29:51.053 --> 01:29:53.055
Why don't you help Potter
put his books back.

01:30:01.688 --> 01:30:03.941
You know,
if you're interested in plants...

01:30:04.149 --> 01:30:06.652
...you'd be better off with
Goshawk's Guide to Herbology.

01:30:07.236 --> 01:30:11.532
Do you know there's a wizard in Nepal
who's growing gravity-resistant trees?

01:30:11.698 --> 01:30:15.452
Neville, no offense,
but I really don't care...

01:30:16.203 --> 01:30:17.830
...about plants.

01:30:18.247 --> 01:30:19.915
Now, if there's...

01:30:20.082 --> 01:30:24.837
...a Tibetan turnip that will allow me
to breathe underwater for an hour...

01:30:25.087 --> 01:30:27.464
...then great. But otherwise--

01:30:27.673 --> 01:30:31.343
I don't know about a turnip.
But you could always use gillyweed.

01:30:32.636 --> 01:30:35.264
-Any bets? Any bets?
-Come on, place your bets!

01:30:35.514 --> 01:30:36.974
Step up, mates! Don't be shy.

01:30:37.057 --> 01:30:38.600
-Three lads.
-One lady.

01:30:38.767 --> 01:30:40.978
-Four go down.
-But do four come up?

01:30:41.270 --> 01:30:42.813
Don't be so mean.

01:30:43.355 --> 01:30:45.274
-Any bets?
-Fleur's 10-1.

01:30:47.276 --> 01:30:49.361
HARRY: You're sure about this, Neville?
-Absolutely.

01:30:49.570 --> 01:30:51.488
HARRY: For an hour?
-Most likely.

01:30:51.697 --> 01:30:53.198
Most likely?

01:30:53.282 --> 01:30:55.492
Well, there is some debate
among herbologists...

01:30:55.742 --> 01:30:58.203
...as to the effects of fresh water
versus salt water--

01:30:58.287 --> 01:31:01.123
You're telling me this now?
You must be joking!

01:31:01.290 --> 01:31:03.208
I just wanted to help.

01:31:03.292 --> 01:31:06.378
Well, that makes you a right sight
better than Ron and Hermione.

01:31:06.587 --> 01:31:08.297
Where are they anyway?

01:31:08.505 --> 01:31:11.508
-You seem a little tense, Harry.
-Do I?

01:31:18.515 --> 01:31:20.851
DUMBLEDORE:
Welcome to the second task.

01:31:21.018 --> 01:31:24.646
Last night, something was stolen
from each of our champions.

01:31:24.855 --> 01:31:26.231
A treasure of sorts.

01:31:26.315 --> 01:31:29.026
These four treasures,
one for each champion...

01:31:29.276 --> 01:31:31.904
...now lie on the bottom
of the Black Lake.

01:31:32.154 --> 01:31:33.614
In order to win...

01:31:33.780 --> 01:31:37.618
...each champion need only find
their treasure and return to the surface.

01:31:37.784 --> 01:31:40.370
-Simple enough, except for this:
-Put that in your mouth.

01:31:40.537 --> 01:31:44.249
They will have but one hour to do so,
and one hour only.

01:31:44.333 --> 01:31:48.337
After that, they'll be on their own.
No magic will save them.

01:31:48.795 --> 01:31:51.173
You may begin
at the sound of the cannon.

01:32:17.574 --> 01:32:20.452
-What's the matter with him?
-I don't know, I can't see him.

01:32:21.912 --> 01:32:24.831
Oh, my God.
I've killed Harry Potter.

01:32:26.708 --> 01:32:28.585
SEAMUS:
Yeah!

01:32:29.795 --> 01:32:31.380
What?

01:33:29.896 --> 01:33:31.106
Oh!

01:33:50.917 --> 01:33:53.170
DUMBLEDORE: The Beauxbatons
champion, Miss Delacour...

01:33:53.420 --> 01:33:55.797
...has unfortunately
been forced to retire...

01:33:56.465 --> 01:33:59.509
...so she will take no further part
in this task.

01:35:17.504 --> 01:35:19.214
But she's my friend too!

01:35:20.757 --> 01:35:22.551
Only one!

01:36:13.810 --> 01:36:15.687
Let's get down below.

01:36:25.697 --> 01:36:28.617
[CHANTING]
Krum! Krum! Krum!

01:37:26.132 --> 01:37:27.759
-Yes!
-Whoo!

01:37:45.902 --> 01:37:48.029
Ascendio!

01:37:53.285 --> 01:37:54.911
Harry!

01:37:57.289 --> 01:37:58.707
He's all right.

01:37:59.916 --> 01:38:01.418
He's all right. Barty!

01:38:01.668 --> 01:38:04.921
SEAMUS: Go get him another towel.
-I want all the judges over here now!

01:38:05.672 --> 01:38:09.009
You saved her, even though
she wasn't yours to save.

01:38:09.718 --> 01:38:11.428
My little sister.

01:38:11.761 --> 01:38:13.430
Thank you.

01:38:14.180 --> 01:38:16.808
And you! You helped.

01:38:17.684 --> 01:38:20.687
Well, yeah, a bit.

01:38:26.026 --> 01:38:27.652
Merci.

01:38:27.736 --> 01:38:28.945
-Harry!
-Hermione! Ow.

01:38:29.154 --> 01:38:31.740
Are you all right? You must be freezing.

01:38:33.033 --> 01:38:34.951
Personally, I think
you behaved admirably.

01:38:35.160 --> 01:38:37.787
I finished last, Hermione. Ah!

01:38:37.954 --> 01:38:42.167
Next to last.
Fleur never got past the Grindylows.

01:38:42.334 --> 01:38:45.670
KARKAROFF:
Krum! Krum! Krum!

01:38:45.754 --> 01:38:48.715
-Come on! Come on!
-Attention!

01:38:50.842 --> 01:38:53.678
Attention!

01:38:53.970 --> 01:38:57.849
The winner is Mr. Diggory...

01:38:58.350 --> 01:39:01.770
...who showed innate command
of the Bubble-Head Charm.

01:39:01.978 --> 01:39:04.689
However, seeing as Mr. Potter
would have finished first...

01:39:04.773 --> 01:39:09.778
...had it not been for his determination
to rescue not only Mr. Weasley...

01:39:09.861 --> 01:39:14.240
...but the others as well,
we've agreed to award him...

01:39:14.491 --> 01:39:15.992
...second place...

01:39:16.242 --> 01:39:17.994
-Yes!
-Second place!

01:39:18.244 --> 01:39:20.830
...for outstanding moral fiber!

01:39:22.123 --> 01:39:23.792
Yes!

01:39:24.376 --> 01:39:25.502
Oh!

01:39:27.379 --> 01:39:28.880
-Right on.
-All that moral fiber, eh?

01:39:29.130 --> 01:39:30.799
-It's great.
-Moral fiber?

01:39:30.882 --> 01:39:33.343
Blimey. Even when you go wrong,
it turns out right.

01:39:33.510 --> 01:39:36.137
-Yeah, well done, Moral Fiber.
-Congratulations, Potter.

01:39:36.346 --> 01:39:37.889
-A fine achievement.
-Thank you.

01:39:38.139 --> 01:39:39.724
Well done, boy.

01:39:39.808 --> 01:39:43.103
RON: See you at Hagrid's, Harry.
CROUCH: I'm sorry we haven't spoken.

01:39:43.269 --> 01:39:47.273
After all, your story is one
I've heard so many times.

01:39:48.274 --> 01:39:51.778
Quite remarkable, really.
Tragic, of course...

01:39:51.861 --> 01:39:53.822
...to lose one's family.

01:39:55.865 --> 01:39:58.034
Never whole again, are we?

01:40:00.370 --> 01:40:02.414
Still, life goes on...

01:40:03.039 --> 01:40:04.833
...and here we stand.

01:40:07.794 --> 01:40:10.380
I'm sure your parents would be
very proud of you today, Potter.

01:40:10.547 --> 01:40:11.923
Bartemius!

01:40:12.173 --> 01:40:16.302
Not trying to lure Potter into one of the
Ministry's summer internships, are we?

01:40:16.553 --> 01:40:19.848
The last boy who went into the
Department of Mysteries never came out!

01:40:32.152 --> 01:40:33.945
And they say I'm mad.

01:40:43.329 --> 01:40:46.958
Now, I remember--
I remember when I first met you all.

01:40:47.208 --> 01:40:50.211
Biggest bunch of misfits
I ever set eyes on.

01:40:50.879 --> 01:40:53.339
Suppose you remind me
of meself a little.

01:40:53.590 --> 01:40:57.594
-And here we all are, four years later.
-We're still a bunch of misfits.

01:40:57.844 --> 01:41:00.972
Well, maybe,
but we've all got each other.

01:41:01.222 --> 01:41:02.807
And Harry, of course.

01:41:02.891 --> 01:41:08.354
Soon to be the youngest
Triwizard champion there's ever been!

01:41:08.605 --> 01:41:10.607
Hooray!

01:41:11.941 --> 01:41:13.359
ALL [SINGING]:
Hogwarts, Hogwarts

01:41:13.568 --> 01:41:14.736
Hoggy Warty Hogwarts

01:41:14.903 --> 01:41:17.322
Teach us something, please

01:41:27.248 --> 01:41:28.875
HARRY:
Mr. Crouch?

01:41:35.757 --> 01:41:37.258
DUMBLEDORE:
A man has died here, Fudge.

01:41:37.467 --> 01:41:39.469
And he won't be the last.
You must take action.

01:41:39.636 --> 01:41:41.137
FUDGE:
I will not.

01:41:41.387 --> 01:41:43.181
In times like these,
the wizard world looks

01:41:43.223 --> 01:41:45.475
to its leaders for strength, Dumbledore!

01:41:45.642 --> 01:41:46.935
DUMBLEDORE:
Then for once show them some!

01:41:47.143 --> 01:41:51.147
The Triwizard Tournament will not be
canceled. I will not be seen as a coward!

01:41:51.397 --> 01:41:54.651
DUMBLEDORE: A true leader does what
is right, no matter what others think.

01:41:54.859 --> 01:41:57.612
-What did you say to me?
MOODY: Excuse me, gentlemen.

01:41:57.779 --> 01:42:01.407
It may interest you to know
this conversation is no longer private.

01:42:05.787 --> 01:42:07.288
Oh, Harry!

01:42:07.497 --> 01:42:09.874
Harry, how good to see you again.

01:42:10.667 --> 01:42:12.043
I can come back later, professor.

01:42:12.252 --> 01:42:15.672
Not necessary, Harry. The minister and I
are done. I'll be back in a moment.

01:42:15.922 --> 01:42:18.383
Minister, after you.

01:42:18.967 --> 01:42:20.927
There you are. Your hat.

01:42:21.010 --> 01:42:24.806
Oh, Harry, do feel free to indulge in
a little Licorice Snap in my absence.

01:42:24.973 --> 01:42:28.017
But I have to warn you,
they're a wee bit sharp.

01:42:54.210 --> 01:42:55.712
Aah!

01:43:59.609 --> 01:44:01.110
Professor?

01:44:01.277 --> 01:44:03.988
-Professor.
-Yeah.

01:44:14.791 --> 01:44:18.544
Igor Karkaroff, you have been brought
from Azkaban at your own request...

01:44:18.795 --> 01:44:20.672
...to present evidence to this council.

01:44:20.922 --> 01:44:23.549
Should your testimony
prove consequential...

01:44:23.758 --> 01:44:27.804
...council may be prepared
to order your immediate release.

01:44:28.054 --> 01:44:32.558
Until such time, you remain in the eyes
of the Ministry a convicted Death Eater.

01:44:32.767 --> 01:44:34.310
Do you accept these terms?

01:44:35.061 --> 01:44:37.647
-I do, sir.
-And what do you wish to present?

01:44:38.106 --> 01:44:40.441
I have names, sir.

01:44:41.109 --> 01:44:44.654
There was Rosier, Evan Rosier.

01:44:47.198 --> 01:44:49.826
-Rosier is dead.
-He took a piece of me with him...

01:44:50.076 --> 01:44:52.120
-...though, didn't he?
KARKAROFF: I didn't know.

01:44:52.203 --> 01:44:55.039
CROUCH: If that is all the witness has--
KARKAROFF: No, no, no.

01:44:55.123 --> 01:44:58.334
There was Rookwood! He was a spy.

01:44:58.584 --> 01:45:01.045
Augustus Rookwood?
Of the Department of Mysteries?

01:45:01.129 --> 01:45:02.213
KARKAROFF:
Yeah, the same.

01:45:02.422 --> 01:45:06.134
He passed information to You-Know-Who
from inside the Ministry itself.

01:45:07.343 --> 01:45:10.680
Very well. Council will deliberate.

01:45:10.847 --> 01:45:12.849
In the meantime,
you will return to Azkaban.

01:45:13.057 --> 01:45:17.687
No! Wait, please! Please, I have more!
What about Snape? Severus Snape?

01:45:17.854 --> 01:45:20.857
As the council is aware,
I've given evidence on this matter.

01:45:21.107 --> 01:45:25.069
Severus Snape was indeed a Death Eater
and, prior to Lord Voldemort's downfall...

01:45:25.153 --> 01:45:26.571
-...turned spy for us at
great personal risk.

01:45:26.654 --> 01:45:28.156
KARKAROFF: It's a lie!

01:45:28.239 --> 01:45:31.826
-Today he's no more a Death Eater than I.
-Snape remains faithful to the Dark Lord!

01:45:31.993 --> 01:45:34.162
Silence!

01:45:34.871 --> 01:45:38.166
Unless the witness possesses
any genuine name of consequence...

01:45:38.374 --> 01:45:40.501
...this session is now concluded.

01:45:40.710 --> 01:45:42.754
Oh, no, no, no.

01:45:43.713 --> 01:45:45.173
I've heard about one more.

01:45:45.256 --> 01:45:48.009
CROUCH: What's that?
-The name.

01:45:48.176 --> 01:45:49.510
-Yes?
-I know for a fact...

01:45:49.719 --> 01:45:51.763
...this person took part
in the capture...

01:45:52.013 --> 01:45:54.098
...and, by means
of the Cruciatus Curse...

01:45:54.182 --> 01:45:57.769
...torture of the Auror Frank Longbottom
and his wife!

01:45:58.019 --> 01:46:00.188
CROUCH: The name.
Give me the wretched name!

01:46:00.396 --> 01:46:01.898
KARKAROFF:
Barty Crouch...

01:46:05.651 --> 01:46:06.736
...Junior.

01:46:16.204 --> 01:46:17.914
MAN:
Hold him down!

01:46:21.501 --> 01:46:25.213
Get your filthy hands off me,
you pathetic little men!

01:46:26.923 --> 01:46:28.424
Hello, Father.

01:46:29.926 --> 01:46:31.928
You are no son of mine.

01:46:43.231 --> 01:46:47.693
Curiosity is not a sin, Harry.
But you should exercise caution.

01:46:49.195 --> 01:46:50.446
It's a Pensieve.

01:46:50.655 --> 01:46:55.243
Very useful if, like me,
you find your mind a wee bit stretched.

01:46:55.451 --> 01:46:59.080
It allows me to see once more
things I've already seen.

01:46:59.455 --> 01:47:02.333
You see, Harry, I have searched
and searched for something...

01:47:02.583 --> 01:47:04.252
...some small detail...

01:47:05.586 --> 01:47:07.713
...something I might have overlooked...

01:47:07.964 --> 01:47:12.218
...something that would explain why
these terrible things have happened.

01:47:12.969 --> 01:47:16.806
Every time I get close to an answer,
it slips away.

01:47:17.849 --> 01:47:19.350
It's maddening.

01:47:21.853 --> 01:47:23.479
Sir? Mr. Crouch's son.

01:47:24.272 --> 01:47:26.315
What exactly happened to him?

01:47:26.482 --> 01:47:31.279
He was sent to Azkaban.
Destroyed Barty to do it.

01:47:32.113 --> 01:47:35.616
But he had no choice.
The evidence was overwhelming.

01:47:37.201 --> 01:47:40.121
-Why do you ask?
-It's just that I....

01:47:40.830 --> 01:47:42.999
I had a dream about him.

01:47:45.293 --> 01:47:48.004
It was in the summer, before school.

01:47:50.256 --> 01:47:53.217
In the dream, I was in a house.

01:47:53.301 --> 01:47:58.222
And Voldemort was there,
only he wasn't quite human.

01:47:58.306 --> 01:48:01.976
And Wormtail was there too.
And Mr. Crouch's son.

01:48:02.226 --> 01:48:04.228
DUMBLEDORE:
Have there been others like this dream?

01:48:04.312 --> 01:48:07.523
Yes. Always the same one.

01:48:10.610 --> 01:48:13.029
Sir, these dreams...

01:48:13.237 --> 01:48:18.326
...what I see, you don't think
it's actually happening, do you?

01:48:19.994 --> 01:48:22.997
I think it's unwise for you
to linger over these dreams, Harry.

01:48:23.372 --> 01:48:25.333
I think it's best if you simply...

01:48:31.047 --> 01:48:32.798
...cast them away.

01:48:42.183 --> 01:48:43.434
KARKAROFF:
It's a sign, Severus.

01:48:44.894 --> 01:48:46.354
You know what it means as well as I.

01:48:54.779 --> 01:48:56.030
Potter!

01:48:56.197 --> 01:48:58.658
What's your hurry?

01:49:03.788 --> 01:49:07.458
Congratulations, your performance
in the Black Lake was inspiring.

01:49:07.708 --> 01:49:10.044
Gillyweed, am I correct?

01:49:10.711 --> 01:49:12.380
Yes, sir.

01:49:13.339 --> 01:49:14.590
Ingenious.

01:49:16.384 --> 01:49:20.388
A rather rare herb, gillyweed.

01:49:21.347 --> 01:49:24.725
Not something found
in your everyday garden.

01:49:26.394 --> 01:49:28.396
Nor is this.

01:49:32.483 --> 01:49:34.360
Know what it is?

01:49:35.486 --> 01:49:36.988
Bubble juice, sir?

01:49:37.488 --> 01:49:39.407
Veritaserum.

01:49:40.241 --> 01:49:43.869
Three drops of this and You-Know-Who
himself would spill his darkest secrets.

01:49:44.120 --> 01:49:49.333
The use of it on a student is,
regrettably, forbidden. However...

01:49:49.875 --> 01:49:52.962
...should you ever steal
from my personal stores again...

01:49:53.129 --> 01:49:57.967
...my hand might just slip over
your morning pumpkin juice.

01:49:58.134 --> 01:50:02.471
-I haven't stolen anything.
-Don't lie to me.

01:50:03.639 --> 01:50:09.437
Gillyweed may be innocuous,
but boomslang skin, lacewing flies?

01:50:10.146 --> 01:50:13.441
You and your little friends are brewing
Polyjuice Potion, and believe me...

01:50:13.524 --> 01:50:15.776
...I'm going to find out why!

01:50:42.553 --> 01:50:44.305
-Yeah!
-Yeah!

01:51:03.491 --> 01:51:04.950
Sonorus!

01:51:09.205 --> 01:51:14.502
Earlier today, Professor Moody placed
the Triwizard Cup deep within the maze.

01:51:14.585 --> 01:51:19.590
Only he knows its exact position.
Now, as Mr. Diggory...

01:51:21.717 --> 01:51:23.511
...and Mr. Potter...

01:51:25.513 --> 01:51:27.223
...are tied for first position...

01:51:27.431 --> 01:51:29.433
...they will be the first to
enter the maze,

01:51:29.517 --> 01:51:31.185
followed by Mr. Krum...

01:51:32.603 --> 01:51:36.232
-...and Miss Delacour.
-Come on! Krum! Krum! Krum!

01:51:37.108 --> 01:51:40.194
DUMBLEDORE: The first person
to touch the cup will be the winner!

01:51:44.532 --> 01:51:47.243
I've instructed the staff
to patrol the perimeter.

01:51:47.493 --> 01:51:50.371
Should, at any point, a contestant wish
to withdraw from the task...

01:51:50.538 --> 01:51:55.000
...he or she need only send up
red sparks with their wands.

01:51:55.376 --> 01:51:59.255
Contestants! Gather around. Quickly!

01:52:02.466 --> 01:52:06.637
In the maze, you'll find no dragons
or creatures of the deep.

01:52:06.846 --> 01:52:10.266
Instead, you'll face something
even more challenging.

01:52:10.516 --> 01:52:13.477
You see, people change in the maze.

01:52:13.561 --> 01:52:15.396
Oh, find the cup if you can.

01:52:15.563 --> 01:52:20.276
But be very wary, you could just
lose yourselves along the way.

01:52:21.652 --> 01:52:24.655
Champions, prepare yourselves!

01:52:33.664 --> 01:52:35.291
Good luck.

01:52:35.583 --> 01:52:37.585
-My boy.
-See you later, Dad.

01:52:39.920 --> 01:52:42.590
On the count of three. One--

01:56:10.339 --> 01:56:11.632
Fleur?

01:56:13.217 --> 01:56:14.760
Fleur.

01:56:18.222 --> 01:56:20.015
Periculum!

01:56:58.804 --> 01:57:00.180
CEDRIC:
Get down!

01:57:00.848 --> 01:57:02.558
Get down!

01:57:03.058 --> 01:57:04.393
Expelliarmus!

01:57:13.902 --> 01:57:17.156
No, don't! Stop!
He's bewitched, Cedric!

01:57:17.322 --> 01:57:19.408
-Get off me!
-He's bewitched!

01:57:30.961 --> 01:57:32.838
HARRY:
Yes.

01:57:53.609 --> 01:57:55.360
Harry!

01:57:57.821 --> 01:57:59.364
Harry!

01:58:01.825 --> 01:58:03.118
Harry!

01:58:05.621 --> 01:58:07.122
Harry!

01:58:09.124 --> 01:58:10.918
Reducto!

01:58:26.642 --> 01:58:30.229
-Th-- Thanks.
-No problem.

01:58:30.646 --> 01:58:35.359
You know, for a moment there,
I thought you were gonna let it get me.

01:58:35.526 --> 01:58:37.236
For a moment, so did I.

01:58:39.029 --> 01:58:40.280
Some game, huh?

01:58:41.281 --> 01:58:42.783
Some game.

01:58:48.038 --> 01:58:49.915
Go!

01:58:59.967 --> 01:59:02.970
Go on, take it.
You saved me, take it!

01:59:03.053 --> 01:59:05.055
-Together. One, two...
-Two...

01:59:05.305 --> 01:59:06.557
-...three!
-...three!

01:59:18.986 --> 01:59:21.989
-You okay?
-Yeah. You?

01:59:28.996 --> 01:59:30.330
Where are we?

01:59:36.003 --> 01:59:37.713
I've been here before.

01:59:41.300 --> 01:59:43.010
It's a Portkey.

01:59:44.845 --> 01:59:49.016
-Harry, the cup is a Portkey.
-I've been here before, in a dream.

01:59:51.018 --> 01:59:54.438
Cedric! We have to get back
to the cup. Now!

01:59:54.605 --> 01:59:56.481
What are you talking about?

02:00:01.862 --> 02:00:04.740
-Harry! What is it?
-Get back to the cup!

02:00:12.331 --> 02:00:14.750
-Who are you? What do you want?
VOLDEMORT: Kill the spare.

02:00:14.958 --> 02:00:17.628
-Avada Kedavra!
-No! Cedric!

02:00:29.014 --> 02:00:30.891
Do it! Now!

02:00:42.778 --> 02:00:45.155
Bone of the father...

02:00:45.405 --> 02:00:47.783
...unwillingly given.

02:00:55.123 --> 02:00:58.168
Flesh of the servant...

02:01:00.170 --> 02:01:03.423
...willingly sacrificed.

02:01:07.552 --> 02:01:11.181
And blood of the enemy...

02:01:17.104 --> 02:01:21.024
-...forcibly taken.
-Oh! Aah! Aah!

02:01:25.654 --> 02:01:28.573
The Dark Lord shall rise...

02:01:29.324 --> 02:01:31.201
-...again.
-Aah!

02:02:34.723 --> 02:02:38.185
My wand, Wormtail.

02:02:47.652 --> 02:02:49.613
Hold out your arm.

02:02:49.780 --> 02:02:51.281
Master.

02:02:51.531 --> 02:02:54.201
Thank you, master.

02:02:54.284 --> 02:02:55.869
The other arm, Wormtail.

02:03:36.326 --> 02:03:38.286
Welcome, my friends.

02:03:39.788 --> 02:03:42.457
Thirteen years it's been, and yet...

02:03:43.250 --> 02:03:48.672
...here you stand before me
as though it were only yesterday.

02:03:49.589 --> 02:03:52.467
I confess myself...

02:03:53.093 --> 02:03:54.553
...disappointed.

02:03:55.262 --> 02:03:57.264
Not one of you tried to find me.

02:03:57.472 --> 02:04:00.934
Crabbe! Macnair!

02:04:01.810 --> 02:04:03.228
Goyle!

02:04:05.605 --> 02:04:07.274
Not even you...

02:04:11.236 --> 02:04:13.113
...Lucius.

02:04:14.948 --> 02:04:19.744
My Lord, had I detected any sign,
a whisper of your whereabouts--

02:04:19.953 --> 02:04:22.956
There were signs, my slippery friend.
And more than whispers.

02:04:23.123 --> 02:04:28.295
I assure you, my Lord,
I have never renounced the old ways.

02:04:30.005 --> 02:04:35.510
The face I have been obliged to present
each day since your absence...

02:04:37.512 --> 02:04:40.307
...that is my true mask.

02:04:40.515 --> 02:04:42.267
I returned.

02:04:44.603 --> 02:04:48.398
Out of fear, not loyalty.

02:04:49.649 --> 02:04:55.363
Still, you have proved yourself useful
these past few months, Wormtail.

02:05:00.619 --> 02:05:03.038
Thank you, master.

02:05:03.538 --> 02:05:05.332
Thank you.

02:05:06.166 --> 02:05:08.251
VOLDEMORT:
Oh. Tsk, tsk, tsk.

02:05:08.335 --> 02:05:10.795
-Such a handsome boy.
HARRY: Don't touch him!

02:05:12.339 --> 02:05:13.757
VOLDEMORT:
Harry.

02:05:13.924 --> 02:05:16.676
I'd almost forgotten you were here.

02:05:16.885 --> 02:05:21.306
Standing on the bones
of my father. Yeah.

02:05:21.389 --> 02:05:22.807
I'd introduce you...

02:05:23.058 --> 02:05:27.354
...but word has it you're almost
as famous as me these days.

02:05:30.023 --> 02:05:32.567
The boy who lived.

02:05:32.817 --> 02:05:35.695
How lies have fed your legend, Harry.

02:05:35.904 --> 02:05:39.908
Shall I reveal what really happened
that night 13 years ago?

02:05:40.075 --> 02:05:44.788
Shall I divulge how
I truly lost my powers?

02:05:44.955 --> 02:05:46.373
Yes, shall I?

02:05:46.915 --> 02:05:48.291
It was love.

02:05:48.375 --> 02:05:52.921
You see, when dear, sweet Lily Potter
gave her life for her only son...

02:05:53.088 --> 02:05:55.590
...she provided the ultimate protection.

02:05:56.091 --> 02:05:57.842
I could not touch him.

02:05:59.094 --> 02:06:01.304
It was old magic.

02:06:01.388 --> 02:06:03.598
Something I should have foreseen.

02:06:03.848 --> 02:06:05.600
But no matter, no matter.

02:06:05.809 --> 02:06:08.061
Things have changed.

02:06:08.728 --> 02:06:12.357
I can touch you...

02:06:12.857 --> 02:06:14.484
...now.

02:06:22.742 --> 02:06:24.119
Yeah.

02:06:30.417 --> 02:06:34.129
Astonishing what a few drops
of your blood will do, eh, Harry?

02:06:35.422 --> 02:06:37.007
Pick up your wand, Potter.

02:06:38.508 --> 02:06:40.844
I said, pick it up! Get up! Get up!

02:06:42.429 --> 02:06:44.723
You've been taught how to duel,
I presume, yes?

02:06:44.889 --> 02:06:47.350
First, we bow to each other.

02:06:47.434 --> 02:06:49.894
Come on, now, Harry.
The niceties must be observed.

02:06:50.145 --> 02:06:53.356
Dumbledore wouldn't want you
to forget your manners, would he?

02:06:53.440 --> 02:06:54.774
I said, bow.

02:06:56.526 --> 02:07:00.989
-That's better. And now....
-No.

02:07:01.448 --> 02:07:03.366
Crucio!

02:07:05.660 --> 02:07:07.454
Crucio!

02:07:08.455 --> 02:07:10.457
Attaboy, Harry.

02:07:10.540 --> 02:07:12.751
Your parents would be proud.

02:07:13.126 --> 02:07:16.463
Especially your filthy Muggle mother.

02:07:16.546 --> 02:07:18.298
Expelliar--

02:07:21.301 --> 02:07:23.553
I'm going to kill you, Harry Potter.

02:07:23.803 --> 02:07:25.805
I'm going to destroy you.

02:07:28.016 --> 02:07:33.521
After tonight, no one will ever again
question my powers.

02:07:34.314 --> 02:07:36.775
After tonight, if they speak of you...

02:07:36.941 --> 02:07:39.569
...they'll speak only of how you...

02:07:39.944 --> 02:07:41.696
...begged for death.

02:07:41.946 --> 02:07:45.575
And I, being a merciful Lord...

02:07:46.326 --> 02:07:47.827
...obliged.

02:07:48.203 --> 02:07:49.579
Get up!

02:07:54.584 --> 02:07:56.586
Don't you turn your back on me,
Harry Potter!

02:07:56.795 --> 02:07:59.089
I want you to look at me
when I kill you!

02:07:59.339 --> 02:08:02.509
I want to see the light
leave your eyes!

02:08:16.481 --> 02:08:18.191
Have it your way.

02:08:19.234 --> 02:08:21.528
-Expelliarmus!
-Avada Kedavra!

02:08:39.087 --> 02:08:41.631
Do nothing! He's mine to finish!

02:08:46.386 --> 02:08:48.012
He's mine!

02:09:21.129 --> 02:09:25.133
Harry, when the connection is broken,
you must get to the Portkey.

02:09:25.300 --> 02:09:27.427
We can linger for a moment
to give you some time...

02:09:27.594 --> 02:09:29.304
...but only a moment.
Do you understand?

02:09:30.555 --> 02:09:33.516
CEDRIC:
Harry, take my body back, will you?

02:09:33.600 --> 02:09:36.269
Take my body back to my father.

02:09:37.312 --> 02:09:38.605
Let go.

02:09:39.063 --> 02:09:41.024
Sweetheart, you're ready.

02:09:41.816 --> 02:09:44.569
Let go! Let go!

02:09:50.283 --> 02:09:51.618
Accio!

02:09:57.332 --> 02:09:59.334
No!

02:10:12.055 --> 02:10:13.640
AMOS:
He did it!

02:10:15.099 --> 02:10:16.643
DUMBLEDORE:
Harry!

02:10:19.354 --> 02:10:20.730
Harry!

02:10:21.981 --> 02:10:25.318
No! No! No, don't!

02:10:25.652 --> 02:10:27.487
For God's sake, Dumbledore,
what's happened?

02:10:27.654 --> 02:10:30.365
He's back. He's back.

02:10:30.573 --> 02:10:32.575
Voldemort's back.

02:10:32.659 --> 02:10:35.078
Cedric, he asked me
to bring his body back.

02:10:35.245 --> 02:10:37.580
I couldn't leave him, not there.

02:10:37.664 --> 02:10:40.583
It's all right, Harry. It's all right.

02:10:40.667 --> 02:10:43.002
He's home. You both are.

02:10:43.211 --> 02:10:46.756
Keep everybody in their seats.
A boy has just been killed.

02:10:49.759 --> 02:10:53.596
The body must be moved, Dumbledore.
There are too many people.

02:10:53.763 --> 02:10:55.598
Let me through.

02:10:55.682 --> 02:10:57.225
Let me through!

02:10:59.143 --> 02:11:00.395
Let me through!

02:11:00.645 --> 02:11:01.896
That's my son!

02:11:03.273 --> 02:11:04.691
That's my boy!

02:11:07.652 --> 02:11:10.280
It's my boy!

02:11:13.032 --> 02:11:16.661
-Come on. Get up. Easy, easy!
-No.

02:11:16.744 --> 02:11:19.706
This is not where you want to be
right now. Come on.

02:11:20.540 --> 02:11:22.709
No!

02:11:25.712 --> 02:11:28.131
It's all right, I got you.

02:11:28.298 --> 02:11:31.718
I got you. Come on. Easy, now.

02:11:35.722 --> 02:11:37.432
AMOS:
No!

02:11:38.641 --> 02:11:40.435
No!

02:12:22.769 --> 02:12:24.604
Are you all right, Potter?

02:12:25.063 --> 02:12:26.981
Does it hurt? That?

02:12:27.190 --> 02:12:28.858
Not so much now.

02:12:29.859 --> 02:12:31.986
Perhaps I'd better take a look at it.

02:12:35.114 --> 02:12:37.116
HARRY:
The cup was a Portkey.

02:12:39.786 --> 02:12:41.788
Someone had bewitched it.

02:12:41.871 --> 02:12:43.998
What was it like?

02:12:44.457 --> 02:12:46.000
-What was he like?
-Who?

02:12:46.250 --> 02:12:47.877
The Dark Lord.

02:12:48.461 --> 02:12:49.796
HARRY:
Aah!

02:12:50.338 --> 02:12:53.466
What was it like
to stand in his presence?

02:12:54.759 --> 02:12:56.511
I don't know.

02:12:59.347 --> 02:13:02.266
It was like I'd fallen
into one of my dreams...

02:13:05.228 --> 02:13:07.230
...into one of my nightmares.

02:13:25.873 --> 02:13:27.542
Were there others?

02:13:27.792 --> 02:13:29.544
In the graveyard, were there others?

02:13:29.752 --> 02:13:31.254
Um....

02:13:33.840 --> 02:13:35.299
I....

02:13:35.925 --> 02:13:39.846
I don't think I said anything
about a graveyard, professor.

02:13:47.311 --> 02:13:50.690
[IMITATING HAGRID] "Marvelous
creatures, dragons, aren't they?"

02:13:54.944 --> 02:13:58.072
Did you think that oaf
would've led you into the woods...

02:13:58.281 --> 02:14:00.158
...if I hadn't suggested it?

02:14:03.828 --> 02:14:07.415
Do you think Cedric Diggory would've
told you to open the egg underwater...

02:14:07.582 --> 02:14:09.959
...if I hadn't told him first myself?

02:14:11.794 --> 02:14:14.338
Did you think Neville Longbottom,
the witless wonder...

02:14:14.589 --> 02:14:17.800
...could've provided you with gillyweed
if I hadn't given him the book...

02:14:17.884 --> 02:14:19.469
...that led him straight to it? Huh?

02:14:21.554 --> 02:14:22.889
Eh?

02:14:27.894 --> 02:14:31.898
It was you from the beginning.
You put my name in the Goblet of Fire.

02:14:32.440 --> 02:14:33.983
You bewitched Krum, but you--

02:14:34.233 --> 02:14:35.985
[MOCKING]
"But-- But--"

02:14:36.235 --> 02:14:38.446
You won because I made it so, Potter.

02:14:38.988 --> 02:14:42.617
You ended up in that graveyard tonight
because it was meant to be so.

02:14:42.825 --> 02:14:43.951
And now the deed is done.

02:14:45.745 --> 02:14:49.957
The blood that runs through these veins
runs within the Dark Lord.

02:14:58.591 --> 02:15:01.969
Imagine how he will reward me
when he learns...

02:15:02.929 --> 02:15:05.473
...that I have once and for all...

02:15:06.015 --> 02:15:10.394
...silenced the great Harry Potter.

02:15:10.645 --> 02:15:11.938
DUMBLEDORE:
Expelliarmus!

02:15:16.609 --> 02:15:17.902
Severus.

02:15:20.947 --> 02:15:22.782
DUMBLEDORE:
That's it, take it.

02:15:23.866 --> 02:15:27.161
-Do you know who I am?
-Albus Dumbledore.

02:15:27.411 --> 02:15:30.039
-Are you Alastor Moody? Are you?
-No.

02:15:30.248 --> 02:15:33.376
Is he in this room? Is he in this room?

02:15:36.420 --> 02:15:37.964
Harry, away from there!

02:15:58.985 --> 02:16:02.196
DUMBLEDORE: You all right, Alastor?
-I'm sorry, Albus.

02:16:03.197 --> 02:16:05.283
That's Moody. But then who's--?

02:16:07.034 --> 02:16:08.077
Polyjuice Potion.

02:16:08.327 --> 02:16:11.664
Now we know who's been stealing
from your stores, Severus.

02:16:11.956 --> 02:16:13.207
We'll get you up in a minute.

02:16:47.742 --> 02:16:49.619
-Aah!
-Harry!

02:16:53.080 --> 02:16:55.499
Barty Crouch Junior.

02:16:55.750 --> 02:16:58.711
I'll show you mine
if you show me yours.

02:17:01.047 --> 02:17:02.131
Your arm, Harry.

02:17:06.594 --> 02:17:08.888
CROUCH JUNIOR:
You know what this means, don't you?

02:17:09.764 --> 02:17:11.057
He's back.

02:17:12.141 --> 02:17:14.393
Lord Voldemort has returned.

02:17:15.269 --> 02:17:17.730
I'm sorry, sir. I couldn't help it.

02:17:17.980 --> 02:17:22.401
Send an owl to Azkaban. I think
they'll find they're missing a prisoner.

02:17:22.985 --> 02:17:25.363
-I'll be welcomed back like a hero.
DUMBLEDORE: Perhaps.

02:17:26.030 --> 02:17:28.908
Personally, I've never had much time
for heroes.

02:17:48.761 --> 02:17:51.305
Today, we acknowledge...

02:17:52.098 --> 02:17:54.934
...a really terrible loss.

02:17:57.061 --> 02:17:59.772
Cedric Diggory was, as you all know...

02:17:59.939 --> 02:18:02.149
...exceptionally hard-working...

02:18:03.109 --> 02:18:05.444
...infinitely fair-minded...

02:18:06.112 --> 02:18:08.322
...and, most importantly...

02:18:08.656 --> 02:18:13.160
...a fierce, fierce friend.

02:18:14.328 --> 02:18:18.791
Now, I think, therefore, you have
the right to know exactly how he died.

02:18:21.836 --> 02:18:23.212
You see...

02:18:24.130 --> 02:18:26.173
...Cedric Diggory was murdered...

02:18:27.133 --> 02:18:29.135
...by Lord Voldemort!

02:18:31.137 --> 02:18:34.598
The Ministry of Magic
does not wish me to tell you this.

02:18:35.182 --> 02:18:39.061
But not to do so, I think,
would be an insult to his memory.

02:18:41.147 --> 02:18:42.857
Now, the pain...

02:18:43.065 --> 02:18:46.610
...we all feel at this dreadful loss
reminds me...

02:18:46.861 --> 02:18:48.154
...and reminds us...

02:18:48.237 --> 02:18:52.074
...that while we may come from different
places and speak in different tongues...

02:18:52.158 --> 02:18:55.619
...our hearts beat as one.

02:18:56.162 --> 02:18:58.164
In light of recent events...

02:18:58.456 --> 02:19:00.750
...the bonds of friendship we've made

02:19:00.791 --> 02:19:03.377
this year will be
more important than ever.

02:19:04.211 --> 02:19:09.633
Remember that, and Cedric Diggory
will not have died in vain.

02:19:10.134 --> 02:19:12.178
You remember that...

02:19:12.845 --> 02:19:15.890
...and we'll celebrate a boy who was...

02:19:16.265 --> 02:19:18.893
...kind and honest...

02:19:19.268 --> 02:19:24.023
...and brave and true,
right to the very end.

02:19:49.215 --> 02:19:51.217
I never liked these curtains.

02:19:51.801 --> 02:19:54.428
Set them on fire in my fourth year.

02:19:54.804 --> 02:19:56.639
By accident, of course.

02:20:02.228 --> 02:20:06.690
I put you in terrible danger
this year, Harry. I'm sorry.

02:20:10.194 --> 02:20:11.779
Professor...

02:20:12.071 --> 02:20:15.074
...when I was in the graveyard,
there was a moment...

02:20:15.783 --> 02:20:20.246
...when Voldemort's wand and mine
sort of connected.

02:20:21.789 --> 02:20:24.208
Priori Incantatem.

02:20:28.254 --> 02:20:30.965
You saw your parents that night,
didn't you?

02:20:31.465 --> 02:20:33.300
They reappeared.

02:20:34.844 --> 02:20:38.597
No spell can reawaken the dead, Harry.
I trust you know that.

02:20:41.267 --> 02:20:43.811
Dark and difficult times lie ahead.

02:20:44.270 --> 02:20:49.191
Soon we must all face the choice
between what is right and what is easy.

02:20:52.361 --> 02:20:54.196
But remember this:

02:20:54.280 --> 02:20:56.282
You have friends here.

02:20:58.284 --> 02:20:59.994
You're not alone.

02:21:20.639 --> 02:21:22.349
Hermione.

02:21:22.850 --> 02:21:24.852
This is for you.

02:21:25.352 --> 02:21:27.605
Write to me. Promise.

02:21:28.731 --> 02:21:30.232
Bye.

02:21:36.322 --> 02:21:38.324
Au revoir, Ron.

02:22:22.326 --> 02:22:24.787
Do you think we'll ever just have
a quiet year at Hogwarts?

02:22:24.954 --> 02:22:26.080
-No.
-No.

02:22:26.330 --> 02:22:30.584
No, I didn't think so. Oh, well.
What's life without a few dragons?

02:22:35.089 --> 02:22:37.841
Everything's going to change now,
isn't it?

02:22:45.224 --> 02:22:46.600
Yes.

02:22:51.397 --> 02:22:54.608
Promise you'll write this summer.
Both of you.

02:22:54.858 --> 02:22:57.403
I won't. You know I won't.

02:22:58.612 --> 02:23:01.740
-Harry will, won't you?
-Yeah. Every week.
